Anh.raw:
{{swp|vi:}}

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{hmp|vi|anh}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-Anh.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Etymology 1===
{{vi-etym-sino|英}}. As for the country name, contracted from {{der|vi|zh|英國|tr={{m|vi|Anh quốc}}||{{l|en|United Kingdom}}}}, from {{der|vi|zh|英|tr=Anh}} (as in {{der|vi|cmn|英吉利|tr=Yīngjílì, Anh Cát Lợi||{{l|en|England}}}} or {{m|cmn|英格蘭|tr=Yīnggélán, Anh Cách Lan||England}}) + {{m|zh|國|tr=quốc||{{l|en|country}}}}.

====Proper noun====
{{vi-propn|head=[[anh|Anh]]}}

# {{given name|vi|unisex|from=Chinese}}
# {{tcl|vi|United Kingdom|id=Q145}}
#: {{ux|vi|Vương quốc '''Anh'''|[[United Kingdom]]}}
# {{tcl|vi|Great Britain|id=Q23666}}
#: {{ux|vi|Vương quốc Liên hiệp '''Anh''' và Bắc Ai-len|[[United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland]]}}
# {{tcl|vi|England|id=Q21}}
#: {{ux|vi|'''Anh''' quốc|England}}
#: {{ux|vi|đội tuyển bóng đá '''Anh'''|{{w|England national football team}}}}

====Adjective====
{{vi-adj|head=[[anh|Anh]]}}

# {{demonym-adj|vi|the <<c/United Kingdom>>|t=British}}
#: {{ux|vi|[[tiếng Anh]] '''Anh'''|British English}}
# {{demonym-adj|vi|<<cc/England>>|t=English}}
#: {{ux|vi|tiếng '''Anh''' Anh|British English}}

====Usage notes====
* More often than not, the average Vietnamese person is not aware of the differences between the United Kingdom, Great Britain and England, and they do not usually attempt to be, similarly to a Chinese person to {{m|zh|英國}} or a Japanese person to {{m|ja|イギリス|tr=Igirisu}}. But unlike in Chinese and Japanese, there seem to be no ''de facto'' distinguishing terms for those concepts in Vietnamese even in diplomatic contexts, although one may sometimes hear {{m|vi|Anh Quốc}} be used for the United Kingdom.
* Due to this name awkwardly being homophonous with {{m|vi|anh||elder brother}}, people who bear it may be preferably referred to also by their middle name, e.g. '''''Tuấn''' Anh'', '''''Lan''' Anh''.

====See also====
