Bình Định.raw:
{{swp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
{{vi-etym-sino|平定|{{l|en|subjugation}}}}.

This land was the birthplace of the [[Tây Sơn]] brothers, who overthrew both the Nguyễn lords of [[Đàng Trong]] and the Trịnh lords of [[Đàng Ngoài]]. After {{lw|vi|Nguyễn Ánh}}, the first emperor of the Nguyễn dynasty, reclaimed the throne of Đại Việt in 1799, the region was renamed '''Bình Định''' ({{lit|subjugation|nocap=1}}) to symbolize the Nguyễn's ultimate triumph over the rebellious Tây Sơn.

