Cuội.raw:
===Etymology===
{{lw|vi|Nguyễn Đổng Chi}} stated that Cuội, the man sitting under a tree in the Moon, had been a different folkloric person than Cuội, the habitually lying man or boy; yet those two eventually merged into one, becoming a habitually lying man or boy sitting under a tree in the Moon.<ref>{{cite-book|author= Nguyễn Đổng Chi|year= 2000|title= Kho tàng truyện cổ tích Việt Nam|volume= I (collections I, II, III)|pages= 457, 903}}</ref> 

According to {{lw|vi|Nguyễn Hùng Vĩ}}:
* The Man in the Moon's name ''Cuội'' is related to {{cog|vi|cội||roots}} and element ''cối'' (from {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*koːjʔ||[[plant]]; [[vegetation]]}} and fossilized in {{m|vi|cây cối|cây '''cối'''}});<ref name = "nhv">{{cite-web|year= 2014|work= Văn Việt|author= Nguyễn Hùng Vĩ|title= Từ điển cũng... cuội|url= https://vanviet.info/nghien-cuu-phe-binh/tu-dien-cung-cuoi/}}</ref>
* The folkloric habitual liar's name ''Cuội'' is a {{vi-etym-sino|拐|to abduct; to misappropriate|quải|hv=n|nocap= y}};<ref name = "nhv"/> 
** Vĩ also notes that the folkloric habitual liar's proper name once became a generic noun denoting a habitual liar, recorded as «''quội''» in {{w|Alexandre de Rhodes}}'s ''{{w|Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum}}'';<ref>{{cite-book|author= w:Alexandre de Rhodes|title= w:Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum|year=  1651|page= 627-628|pageurl= https://vi.wikisource.org/wiki/Trang%3ADictionarium_Annamiticum_Lusitanum_et_Latinum_(Bayerische_Staatsbibliothek).pdf/324}}</ref><ref name = "nhv"/> 
** He also critiques many lexicographers like {{w|Pierre Pigneau de Behaine}}, Gustave Hue, Georges Cordier, J. F. M. Génibrel, {{w|Huỳnh Tịnh Của}}, and {{w|Trương Vĩnh Ký}} for mistakenly glossing «''cuội''» as "echo".<ref name = "nhv"/>
* Neither is related to {{m|vi|cuội||pebble}}.<ref name = "nhv"/>

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{hmp|vi|cuội}}

===Proper noun===
{{vi-propn|head=[[cuội|Cuội]]}}

# {{lb|vi|folklore}} a man sitting under a tree in the moon {{q|inspired by a {{w|Lunar pareidolia|lunar pareidolia}}}}
