Cái Răng.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
According to [[folk etymology]], the name originates from a story that in the early days of the Vietnamese settlement, there was a very large crocodile washed up here, its teeth stuck on this land.

In ''Tự vị tiếng nói miền Nam'' by {{lw|vi|Vương Hồng Sển}}, the name is said to be derived from {{der|vi|km|ចង្ក្រាន||stove, furnace}} (whence also {{m|vi|cà ràng}}). The Khmers in Xà Tôn ({{l|vi|Tri Tôn}}) used to make and sell their own kind of furnaces. Over time, people started to pronounce ''kraan'' as ''Cái Răng''.

