{{vi-ref|Trần Trọng Dương (2013)}} considers this a disyllabic derivation of the proto-Vietnamese form he provisionally reconstructed as {{IPAfont|/*klù/}}. It is likely a {{doublet|vi|sấu|nocap=1}}, and therefore, {{der+|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*k-ruːʔ|nocap=1|t=crocodile}} (Ferlus, 2007). The meaning of the hydronym, then, could be roughly translated as “crocodile(-infested) river”.

For other case of disyllabic derivation in Vietnamese, see {{m|vi|thằn lằn}}, {{m|vi|thốt nốt}}, etc.

