Cát Hải.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
{{blend|vi|Cát Bà|hải}}. ''Cát Bà'' is the largest island of the district.

* According to [[folk etymology]], ''Cát Bà'' is a "misread" of {{m|vi|[[các]] [[bà]]||ladies}}. During the {{m|vi|Trần}} Dynasty, the women here took care of the logistics for the men to fight during the war. This is very unlikely, since this place is in Northern Vietnam, where there the coda {{IPAfont|/t/-/k/}} merger never happened, unlike placenames like {{m|vi|Cát Lái}} (which is probably indeed {{m|vi|[[các]] [[lái]]||traders}}) in Southern Vietnam, where this merger did actually occur.
* Compared to the nearby island named {{m|vi|Cát Ông}} ({{m|vi|[[các]] [[ông]]||men}}). Possibly modelled after the false "etymology" above.

