Cần Thơ.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
{{unk|vi}}. One theory proposes that this is a corruption of ''Cầm Thi'' in {{m|vi|Cầm Thi Giang|lit=river of poems}}, a poetic name given by {{w|Gia Long}} for a river nearby. Another legend has it that this is a combination of {{com|vi|rau cần|alt1=rau '''cần'''|rau thơm|alt2=rau '''thơm'''|t1=[[water dropwort]]|t2=[[mint]]}}, both products of the Cần Thơ area in ancient times.

The suggestions above are both certainly [[folk etymology|folk etymologies]]. The ''Cần'' in placenames almost always reflects a presyllable of the shape {{IPAfont|kVN-}} in Khmer (where N is a nasal), compare {{m|vi|Cần Giờ}} (from {{ncog|km|កញ្ជើ}}), {{m|vi|Cần Giuộc}} (from {{ncog|km|កន្ទួត}}), {{m|vi|Cần Vọt}}/{{m|vi|Cần Bột}} (from {{ncog|km|កំពត}}). Still, it is not known which specific {{bor|vi|km|-}} item Cần Thơ was borrowed from.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Proper noun===
{{vi-proper noun|head=Cần Thơ|芹苴}}

# {{place|vi|former province|c/Vietnam|t1=Cần Thơ}} (abolished in 2004)
