Cần Giờ.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|vi|km|កញ្ជើ|t=basket}}, as the local people often used "basket boats" to commute.

According to a [[folk etymology]], when [[Nguyễn Ánh]] ran to the land of ''Cần Giờ'' to avoid the [[Tây Sơn]] army. He used big vases of water to make clocks, inside these vases contained water and hung a rod with ink engraved on it, so {{com|vi|cần|t1=rod|giờ|t2=hour}}.

According to another [[folk etymology]], when the merchant ships went to [[Saigon]], to this land, they had to wait a while for the tide to rise, so {{com|vi|cần|t1=to need|giờ|t2=time}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Proper noun===
{{vi-proper noun|head=[[cần|Cần]] [[giờ|Giờ]]}}

# {{place|vi|district|city/Ho Chi Minh City|t1=Cần Giờ}}

