Kẻ Chợ.raw:
[[File:KẻChợ仉𢄂.png|thumb|180px|[[仉#Vietnamese|仉]][[𢄂#Vietnamese|𢄂]] written in 大南國史演歌 Đại Nam quốc sử diễn ca]]

===Etymology===
The demotic name ({{m|vi|tên Nôm}}) for the city, from {{com|vi|kẻ|t1=person; nominalizer|chợ|t2=market}}, roughly "market place". At first, the name refers to the residential area in [[Đông Kinh]], as opposed to the [[w:Imperial Citadel of Thăng Long|Imperial Citadel]]. It was then used to refer to the whole of Đông Kinh.

The name is used since the [[w:Later Lê dynasty|Later Lê dynasty]] by both locals and foreigners.<ref>Nguyễn Ngọc Tiến (2020). [https://nhipsonghanoi.hanoimoi.vn/ke-cho-cai-ten-dan-da-cua-thang-long-624587.html "Kẻ Chợ, cái tên dân dã của Thăng Long"]</ref>

This placename was once used as a common noun, meaning "capital", see {{m|vi|kẻ chợ}}.

