Kon Tum.raw:
{{swp|vi:}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{vi-l|Kông Tum}}

===Etymology===
Explained in some Vietnamese sources as being from a {{bor|vi|bdq|-}} phrase meaning "lake village". However, no such matching elements can be found, the closest is probably {{m|bdq|kơtu||old abandoned village}}. Even using possible "variants" of the first syllable (such as {{m|bdq|kông}} and {{m|bdq|kom}}, Bahnar's vowel length distinction also taken into account) yields little, except for maybe {{m|bdq|akŏm||to meet together, to gather things}}. In Bahnar, "village" is {{m|bdq|pơlei}}, while "lake, pond" is {{m|bdq|dơnŏu}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA|con tum|công tum}}

===Proper noun===
{{vi-proper noun|head=Kon Tum}}

# {{place|vi|former province|c/Vietnam|t1=Kon Tum}} (abolished in 2025)
# {{place|vi|city|c/Vietnam|t1=Kon Tum}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|bor=1|en|Kon Tum}}

Kê Thành.raw:
