{{wp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
From {{m+|vi|nhà bè|t=hut built atop a wooden raft}}. In the past, many people from [[Đàng Ngoài]] went down the boat to the [[Soài Rạp]] River, meet the reverse current, so they built rafts on the river, serving as a place for cooking and living for the whole fleet. Nowadays, "[[nhà bè]]" are only seen in the [[Mekong Delta]] but are no longer seen in [[HCMC]].

