Nẫu.raw:
===Etymology===
Although this spelling is seemingly unetymological, it is more common than {{m|vi|Nẩu}}. The dialects spoken in {{w|Bình Định province|Bình Định}} and {{w|Phú Yên province|Phú Yên}} are Southern so they do have ''hỏi''-''ngã'' merger (a general Southern feature). These dialects generally have lower range of fundamental frequency in semitones across all tones (between 27-39 Hz for all tones in {{w|Hoài Nhơn}}, compared to something like 34-52 Hz in Northern dialects), although it is not totally clear to how this plays into the perception of this merged C tone (''hỏi''-''ngã'') as ''ngã'' (C2) instead of ''hỏi'' (C1).

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Proper noun===
