Rạch Giá.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
From {{com|vi|rạch|giá|t1=[[small]] [[irrigation]] [[canal]]|t2=[[bean sprout]]s}}.

According to another etymology, the city name possibly from {{bor|vi|km|[[ក្រមួន]][[ស]]|t=white wax}}. But, this phonological change lacks conviction. Specifically, {{m|km|ក្រមួន|tr=*kra}} is easier to become {{m|vi|tra|*tra}} / {{m|vi|trác|*trác}} and {{m|km|ស|tr=*sa}} is easier to become {{m|vi|sa|*sa}}. In the Southern dialects, {{m|vi|giá}} is pronounced with a voiced palatal consonant approximant /j/, so it is unlikely that the voiceless /s/ becomes voiced /z/.  (compare {{m|vi|Sóc Trăng}}, {{m|vi|Trà Vinh}}, {{m|vi|Sa Đéc}}, etc).

