====Usage notes====
* {{U:vi:sino}}
* While hyphenation has become virtually obsolescent for non-Sanskrit-based names and terms (for example {{m|vi|Như Lai}} rather than {{m|vi|Như-Lai}} or {{m|vi|Như-lai}}), it persists for Sanskrit-based ones in some writings. Among many hyphenated spellings, there seems to be a predominant division between two Sanskrit morphemes, {{m|vi|Thích-ca}} and {{m|vi||Mâu-ni}}. Fully hyphenated spellings such as {{m|vi|Thích-ca-mâu-ni}} are much rarer. Fully capitalized syllables ({{m|vi|Thích-Ca-Mâu-Ni}}) are also less frequent than only the first syllables of each grouping ({{m|vi|Thích-ca Mâu-ni}}).

