Thủ Dầu Một.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
A minority of researchers entertain the idea that at least some element of the name might derived from a {{der|vi|km|-}} word. However, others think that this is a Vietnamese phrase formed from two elements: {{m|vi|thủ|Thủ|to keep}}, and {{m|vi|Dầu Một}}, formed from a plant name (see {{m|vi|dầu||''Dipterocarpus'' spp.}}) and the numeral "one". 

According to [[folk etymology]], because the military station guarding in {{l|vi|Bình An}} district town was located on a hill with large {{taxfmt|Dipterocarpus|genus}} trees ({{m|vi|[[cây]] [[dầu]]}}), people once called it {{m|vi|Thủ Dầu Miệt}}, in which {{m|vi|Thủ|t=to keep}}, and {{m|vi|miệt}} prefers to plantations (see {{m|vi|miệt vườn}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Proper noun===
{{vi-proper noun}}

# a [[city]] in [[Bình Dương]] province, [[Vietnam]]

