Tàu.raw:
===Alternative forms===
* {{vi-l|tào}}
* {{vi-l|tàu}}
* {{vi-l|Tầu}}
* {{vi-l|tầu}}

===Etymology===
Shortening of {{m|vi|Ba Tàu}}. According to folk etymology, the word {{m|vi|tàu||boat}} was first used to refer to Ming Chinese refugees who fled to Vietnam by boat when the Qing Dynasty took over China. The remnants of Ming Chinese refugees are nowadays known as the {{w|Minh Hương}} people.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{homophones|vi|tàu}}
