Xuất Ê-díp-tô Ký.raw:
===Etymology===
Due to the uncanny resemblance, as well as the peculiarly Japanese-sounding name for Egypt, perhaps {{cal|vi|ja|出エジプト記|tr=Shutsu-Ejiputo-ki|nocap=y|lit=Chronicle of the Departure from Egypt}}. Compare {{cog|zh|出埃及記|tr=Xuất Ai Cập kí}} and {{cog|ko|^출애굽기}}. Most proper names in the Vietnamese Protestant translation of the Bible were derived from French, however, the French title {{ncog|fr|livre de l’[[Exode]]}} seems implausible here since {{m|fr|Exode}} only biblically implies "departure from Egypt", compared to the Catholic title {{m|vi|Xuất hành}} which is more general.  Ê-díp-tô could also be from Portuguese "Egito", as there are many Catholic transliterations from Portuguese, for example, 基移吹蘇 Kirixitô for Portuguese rendition of Christ 'Christo' in Catholic chữ Nôm texts.

