biết.raw:
===Etymology===
Norman and Mei (1976), Schuessler (2007), Sagart (2008): Related to [[Min]] {{cog|zh|捌||to know}} (proto-Min: ''*pat''). The direction of borrowing is debated; Norman and Mei, and Schuessler favour an Austroasiatic origin for this word, and regard Min as a loan. Sagart, on the other hand, proposes that the sense “to know; to recognise” in both Min and Vietnamese is an extension of the sense “to differentiate; to separate” of {{och-l|別|tr={{IPAfont|*N-pret}}}} (B-S), and hence treats V. ''biết'' as a {{vi-etym-sino|別||hv=n|biệt|nocap=1}}, a semantic development shared with Min.

The word has mostly displaced the use of {{m|vi|hay}}, the more commonly seen word for "to know" in older literature.

Also compare {{cog|mkh-ban-pro|*băt||to know}} (Starling).

The Protestant biblical sense is a {{semantic loan|vi|fr|connaître|nocap=y}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{hmp|vi|biếc}} {{qualifier|southern Vietnam}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-biết.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Verb===
{{vi-verb|[[別]], [[捌]], [[𪿍]], [[𲳃]]}}

# to [[know]]; to be [[aware]] of
#* {{quote-book|vi|year=1936|author=[[w:Vũ Trọng Phụng|Trọng Phụng Vũ]]|title=Số đỏ|trans-title={{w|Dumb Luck (novel)|Dumb Luck}}|text=Cụ Hồng lại nhăn mặt lần thứ mười mà khẽ gắt cũng lần thứ mười rằng:<br>— Biết rồi ! Biết rồi ! Khổ lắm, nói mãi !|t=Great-granddad Hồng groans for the 10th time as he grimaces also for the 10th time: "Oh I get it! I get it! Enough with the nagging already!"}}
# to [[learn]] about; to [[realize]]
# to [[know]] how to; to be [[able]] to
#: {{uxi|vi|'''biết''' đọc|'''to be able''' to read}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''biết''' viết|'''to know how''' to write}}
# to have a [[taste]] for (an [[acquired taste]])
#: {{uxi|vi|'''biết''' ăn [[mắm tôm]]|'''to like''' to eat [[shrimp paste]]}}
# {{lb|vi|bible|Protestantism}} to {{l|en|know}} {{gl|have sexual relations with}}

