bánh bò.raw:
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
Shortened from {{m|vi|bánh vú bò|t=cow udder cake}} < {{compound|vi|bánh|t1=cake|alt2=vú bò|t2=cow udder}} < {{compound|vi|vú|t1=breast|bò|t2=cow}}.

According to a popular [[folk etymology]], this term instead comes from {{compound|vi|bánh|bò|tr2=to crawl}}, referring to how the cake "crawls" up to the rim of the bowl when steamed to completion.

