===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*k-biːrʔ|*k-biːrʔ ~ *k-piːrʔ}}, from {{inh|vi|mkh-pro|*cpiir}}. Cognate with {{cog|mtq|pỉl}}, proto-Monic ''*cmpiir'' (modern {{cog|mnw|သ္ပဳ|tr=həpɔe||pumpkin}}), {{cog|ril|-}} ''sᵊpir¹'', {{cog|kjg|-}} [Cuang] ''hmpiːr'' ("melon").

This word was originally referred to some kind of native gourd (pumpkins are from the Americas), most likely the [[wax gourd]], now also commonly called {{m|vi|bí đao}}; or maybe it was (and is still) just the word for cucurbits in general.

