===Etymology===
{{vi-etym-sino|筆|[[writing]] [[brush]], [[pen]]}}. Its relationship with {{m|vi|viết||to write}} is dubious.

Diachronically, this is an early loan that came to be accepted as Sino-Vietnamese. Possibly descends from a regional Old Chinese ancestor which had no *{{IPAfont|/-r-/}} (compare Eastern-Han-period Yan dialectal pronunciation {{och-l|弗|tr= *{{IPAfont|put}}}} (reconstructed by Baxter & Sagart 2014:43) of {{zh-l|*聿}}/{{zh-l|*筆}} [https://ctext.org/shuo-wen-jie-zi/yu-bu2/zh]) and predated the loaning of Sino-{{cog|ko|필(筆)}} and Sino-{{cog|ja|筆|tr=hitsu}}.

Cognate with {{cog|ko|붓}}, a vernacular loan borrowed at around the same time.

