bằng.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-bằng.wav|a=Hanoi}}

===Etymology 1===
{{vi-etym-sino|平|[[level]]; [[even]]}}; originally the Northern reading. Its distribution likely already extended beyond Northern Vietnam by the time Vietnamese started to be written down in the Latin script. See also {{m|vi|bình}}, the current chief form used in compounds and the main form in placenames in Southern Vietnam. 

The expected reading of the Northern form would be ''*bềnh'', which is unattested. Compare pairs such as {{m|vi|bệnh}} vs. {{m|vi|bịnh}}, {{m|vi|nghênh}} vs. {{m|vi|nghinh}}, {{m|vi|lệnh}} vs. {{m|vi|lịnh}}.

It is sometimes claimed that this form is due to the taboo of the title {{vi-l|北平王}} (Bắc Bình vương) of 18th-century monarch [[w:Quang Trung|Quang Trung]]. But this is demonstrably false, as {{m|mkh-mvi|bàng}} (as well as {{m|mkh-mvi|bàng an}} (→ {{m|vi|bằng an}}), {{m|mkh-mvi|bàng ien}} (→ {{m|vi|bằng yên}})) is attested in the 17th-century ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651), a dictionary based chiefly on the dialects of Northern Vietnam. The irregular vowel correspondence is possibly also seen in {{m|vi|thẳng}} (if that were from early {{w|Middle Chinese}} {{ltc-l|侹|id=2}} ← {{och-l|侹|id=2}} (ZS)).<!--- Possibly also cẳng (if that were from Old Chinese 脛 *ɡeːŋs (ZS) ~ *m-kʰˤeŋ-s (B&S)) --->

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|vi|bường|q=Central Vietnam}}
* {{alt|vi|bình|q=Southern Vietnam}}

====Adjective====
