bặt vô âm tín.raw:
===Alternative forms===
* {{l|vi|biệt vô âm tín}}

===Etymology===
Apparently a Vietnamese construct from Sinitic elements: {{m|zh|拔||to pull}}, {{m|zh|無||not have, nothing}}, {{m|zh|音信||news}}. Compare the obsolete/archaic compound {{m|vi|bặt tin||radio silent}}.

The morpheme {{m|vi|bặt}} is of particular interest; its modern "standard" Sino-Vietnamese reading is {{m|vi|bạt}} with long vowel. This "four-character compound" is also attested as {{m|vi|biệt vô âm tín}}; this "alternation" of the first morpheme is also seen in {{m|vi|bặt tăm}} vs. {{m|vi|biệt tăm}}, the latter form probably represents contamination by {{vi-link|biệt|to part, to leave|別}}. Furthermore, some dictionaries (including ''Đại Nam Quấc âm tự vị'' (1895)) defines ''bặt'' as if it is a variant of {{m|vi|bật}}, which is likely a native word; there was probably some more contamination involved.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Idiom===
{{vi-idiom|拔無音信}}

# [[missing]]; [[whereabout]]s [[unknown]]; complete [[radio silent]]
#: {{ux|vi|Nó đi bụi mấy năm trời '''bặt vô âm tín''', vậy mà tuần trước tự nhiên ló mặt về nhà như không.|He ran away, '''not a whit of contact nor news''' for a few years, yet just last week, I saw him at home acting as if nothing happened at all.}}

