bồ hòn.raw:
[[File:Sapindus saponaria var. saponaria (4999557990).jpg|right|thumb|{{uxi|vi|cây '''bồ hòn'''|'''western soapberry''' tree}}|240x240px]]

===Etymology===
Originally meant {{vern|Chinese soapberry}}, a species native to East and Southeast Asia. The meaning was generalised to include the {{vern|western soapberry}} from the {{w|Americas}}.
* The first element ''bồ'' is found in {{m|vi|bồ nâu||{{taxlink|dioscorea cirrhosa|species}}, dyeing yam}}, {{m|vi|bồ quân||{{taxlink|flacourtia jangomas|species}}, Indian coffee plum}}, {{m|vi|bồ hóng||soot}}, {{m|vi|bồ nhìn||scarecrow}}, etc. ({{vi-ref|Vũ Đức Nghiệu, 2019)}}
* The second element ''hòn'' is possibly {{vi-etym-sino|桓|{{vern|Chinese soapberry}}|hoàn|preMC=y|nocap=y}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|head=bồ hòn|cls=[[cây]], [[quả]], [[trái]]|[[蒲𣏒]]}}

