chuồng.raw:
===Etymology===
Uncertain. 

{{zh-ref|Baxter & Sagart (2014)}} proposes that this is borrowed from {{der|vi|och|-}} {{och-l|籠|tr=*k.rˤoŋ}}, thus making it <!--WHAT?--> {{vi-etym-sino|籠||[[lung]], [[lộng]]|hv=n|nocap=y}}. 

[https://evols.library.manoa.hawaii.edu/items/6d1b8d19-4f6f-4251-aae4-2d45e4d12bf3 Alves (2018)] proposes that ''chuồng'' and {{m|vi|lồng}} are doublets and both are early regional loanwords from {{bor|vi|zh|籠}}, yet he is uncertain about connection to Old Chinese {{och-l|籠|tr=*k.rˤoŋ}}; as Old Chinese *''kr-'' regularly yields Vietnamese ‹s-› instead (as in {{m|vi|sức}} & {{m|vi|sen}}). However, ''chuồng''’s initial ‹ch-› might have resulted from another sound change which yields ‹ch-› of {{m|vi|chàng}} & {{m|vi|chạp}}.

See {{zh-l|籠}} for more.

