* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-chèo.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*tʃ-r-ɛːw}}, an {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*-r-|pos=instrumental derivative}} infixed form of {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*tʃɛːw}}, whence Modern {{cog|vi|xeo||to lift up with a crowbar; to propel (a boat) with a long pole}}. Related to {{cog|vi|neo||anchor}}, {{cog|km|ចែវ||to row; paddle}}, {{m|km|ច្រវា||oar; paddle}}, {{cog|lo|ແຊວ||to row}}. Compare {{cog|zh|櫂|tr=trạo}}.

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|cls=[[cây]], [[cái]]|𣛨}}

# [[oar]] or [[paddle]]
#: {{syn|vi|mái|mái chèo}}

====Verb====
{{vi-verb|𢴿}}

# to oar, to paddle

=====See also=====
{{col|vi|chèo chống|chèo kéo|mái chèo}}

===Etymology 2===
Unknown. Theories<ref>https://www.studocu.vn/vn/document/hoc-vien-hanh-chinh/quan-ly-cong/nghe-thuat-san-khau-cheo/65837348</ref> include:
* A deviation from {{l|vi|trào}} as in [[trào phúng]], since the content of the opera is to make fun of bad practices in the contemporary society.
* A deviation from {{l|vi|chầu}}, whose writing in [[chữ Nôm]] include a character for mouth ({{l|zh|口}}) and a character that reads "chầu". See [[hát chầu]].
* A deviation from {{l|vi|chèo}}.
* A deviation from {{l|vi|trò}}.
* From {{l|vi|chèo}} in {{l|vi|chèo}} {{l|vi|thuyền}} (etymology 1).
{{wp|vi:}}

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|掉}}

# {{w|chèo}} {{gloss|traditional Vietnamese opera}}

