From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*ɟuːm}}, from {{inh|vi|mkh-pro|*bɟum}} ~ {{m|mkh-pro|*bɟuum}} ~ {{m|mkh-pro|*bɟuəm}} ~ {{m|mkh-pro|*bɟəm||bunch, to gather together}} (Shorto 2006, #1338); directly cognate with {{m|vi|chòm}}. See also {{m|vi|chụm||to assemble, to gather together}}, {{m|vi|cụm||cluster, bunch}}, {{m|vi|xúm||to form group}}. Probably related to {{m|vi|nhúm}}, {{m|vi|nhóm}} as well (cf. {{cog|mkh-kat-pro|*ɟum||group}}); this would require the initial to be *ʄ, which in fact sometimes alternated with *ɟ.

Compare {{cog|km|ជុំ||to surround, encircle; to assemble, unite, gather together}}, {{cog|bdq|jum||around}}.

