chục.raw:
===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*ɟuːk||ten}}. Cognate with {{cog|aem|-}} ''[[nhcùk]]''. <br>
Attested as {{inh|vi|mkh-mvi|chọuc}} in ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651).<ref>{{quote-web|vi|url=https://vi.wikisource.org/wiki/T%E1%BB%AB_%C4%91i%E1%BB%83n_Vi%E1%BB%87t%E2%80%93B%E1%BB%93%E2%80%93La/C|title=Từ điển Việt–Bồ–La/C|work=Wikisource|date=15-02-2014|passage=chọuc: dezena; decas, adis. một chọuc, hai chọuc:}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-chục.wav|a=Hanoi}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|[[逐]], [[𨔿]], [[𱑐]], [[󰪢]]}}

# [[ten]]
#: {{uxi|vi|một '''chục''' người|'''ten''' men, one '''ten''' of men}}
#: {{uxi|vi|hai '''chục''' người|twen'''ty''' men, two '''tens''' of men}}
#: {{uxi|vi|phần '''chục'''|the first decimal place}}
# {{lb|vi|Mekong Delta}} certain sets of numbers, most usually a [[dozen]] but might be as high as [[eighteen]]

====Usage notes====
* ''Một chục'' is usually used as a synonym of {{m|vi|mười}} (for example, ''một chục người'' is synonymous with ''mười người''). However, ''một'' in ''một chục'' is sometimes dropped in colloquial speech.
* Unlike {{m|vi|mười}}, which is a true numeral, {{m|vi|chục}} is a noun. As a noun, ''chục'' cannot be followed by numerals. *''chục {{m|vi|một}}/{{m|vi|hai}}/''etc. are ungrammatical. For a parallel, compare English {{m|en|crore}} or {{m|en|myriad}}, which are nouns used to denote numbers and can not be directly followed by another numeral.
* Used instead of {{m|vi|mười}} if preceded by {{m|vi|hàng}} (in all senses). *''Hàng mười'' is not natively accepted.
* {{m|vi||chục trứng|ten eggs}} may be used as a unit when concerning purchases of eggs.

