con.raw:
===Etymology===
{{inh+|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*kɔːn}}, from {{inh|vi|aav-pro|*koan}}. Cognate with {{cog|mtq|-}} Bi {{m|mtq|con}}, {{cog|thm|กอน}}, {{cog|mnw|ကွေန်|tr=kon}}, {{cog|km|កូន}}, {{cog|bdq|kon}}, {{cog|kha|khun}}, {{cog|ncb|kōan}}. {{doublet|vi|non|t1=young, juvenile}}, which is from an infixed form of the root.

Attested in ''Phật thuyết đại báo phụ mẫu ân trọng kinh'' (佛說大報父母恩重經, {{circa2|12th cent.|short=1}}) as {{ltc-l|昆}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|côn}}). Attested in the ''Annan Jishi'' (安南即事, 13th century) as {{ltc-l|乾|id=1}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|can}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{hmp|vi|coong}} {{q|Southern Vietnam}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-con.wav|a=Hanoi}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-con.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=đứa|[[𡥵]], [[昆]]}}

# [[child]] {{gloss|daughter or son}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''con''' cái|children}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''con''' nuôi|adopted child}}
#: {{uxi|vi|gà '''con'''|chick}}
#: {{ux|vi|Con cóc con là '''con''' con cóc.|A [[toadlet]] is an offspring of a toad.}}
#* {{quote-book|vi|year=1983|author=Homer|title=Ô-đi-xê|trans-title=The Odyssey|translator=Phan Thị Miến|text=Tê-lê-mác, '''con''' ! Đừng làm rầy mẹ, mẹ còn muốn thử thách cha ở tại nhà này. Thế nào rồi mẹ con cũng sẽ nhận ra, chắc chắn như vậy. Hiện giờ cha còn bẩn thỉu, áo quần rách rưới, nên mẹ con khinh cha, chưa nói : “Đích thị là chàng rồi !”. […]
|translation=Telemachus, my '''son'''! Don’t you bother your mother, she still wants to put me to trials at this home. She will recognize me eventually, there is no doubt about that. I still look like a rascal, in torn clothes, that is why your mother still doubts me, she is yet to say: “It was definitely you this whole time!”. […]}}
# {{lb|vi|rare|chiefly|in translations of ancient texts}} [[son]]
#: {{cot|vi|con gái}}
# {{lb|vi|only in compounds, in fixed expressions}} [[build]]; [[stature]]

====Derived terms====
{{col3|vi|bà con|cháu con|con cái|con cháu|con gái|to con|đô con|nhỏ con|bé con|con trai|con nít|trẻ con|con trẻ|con trăng|con một|con dại cái mang|con nhà tông không giống lông cũng giống cánh|đem con bỏ chợ}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|[[𡥵]], [[昆]]}}

# {{lb|vi|rare|only in compounds}} a [[small]] [[thing]]
#: {{uxi|vi|'''con''' quay|a spinning top}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''con''' lắc|a pendulum}}

====Derived terms====
{{col3|vi|cỏn con|con con}}

====See also====
* {{vi-l|tử}}

===Pronoun===
{{vi-pronoun|[[𡥵]], [[昆]]}}

# [[I]]/[[me]] {{q|used by children when talking to their parents}}
# {{lb|vi|chiefly|_|Central Vietnam|_|and|_|Southern Vietnam}} [[I]]/me {{q|used when talking to someone significantly older than the speaker}}
# [[you]] {{q|used by parents when talking to their children}}
# {{lb|vi|chiefly|_|Central Vietnam|_|and|_|Southern Vietnam}} [[you]] {{q|used when talking to some significantly younger than the speaker}}
#: {{ux|vi|Là '''con''' thật!|It's '''you''' for real!}}

====Usage notes====
* Sense (4) is chiefly used in Central and Southern Vietnam, perhaps extensively to North Central Vietnam. In Northern Vietnam, {{m|vi|cháu}} is used instead. Some Northerners, however, do use ''con'', especially when talking to Southern children on Southern TV shows.

====Synonyms====
* {{s|you (4)}} {{vi-l|cháu}}

===Classifier===
{{vi-cls|[[𡥵]], [[昆]]}}

# {{ng|Indicates animals (including humans).}}
# {{lb|vi|disrespectful}} {{ng|Indicates female people.}}
#: {{ant|vi|thằng}}
#: {{uxi|vi|một thằng, hai '''con'''|one guy, two girls}}
# {{ng|Indicates knives, ships, boats, trains and [[pupil#Noun_2|eye pupils]].}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''con''' dao|a knife}}
# {{ng|Indicates roads, rivers, streams and waves.}}
#: {{uxi|vi|trên '''con''' đường đến hạnh phúc|on the road/path to happiness}}
# {{lb|vi|somewhat|literary}} {{ng|Indicates written characters.}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''con''' chữ|a character or letter}}
# {{lb|vi|colloquial}} {{ng|Indicates any piece of technology, especially with the brand name.}}
## {{ng|Indicates electronic devices.}}
##: {{uxi|vi|'''Con''' Iphone của em đấy.|This is my Iphone.}}
## {{ng|Indicates wheeled vehicles.}}
##: {{ux|vi|Anh mày có hẳn hai '''con''' xe Honda đấy nhớ!|I have two Honda motorbikes!}}
## {{ng|Indicates video games and movies.}}
##: {{ux|vi|Ông chơi '''con''' game này chưa?|Have you played this game?}}

====Usage notes====
* Even though ''con người'' is used, it is generally thought of as a noun phrase on its own, and {{m|vi|người}} does not require a classifier because it is itself a classifier (compare {{cog|ja|人|tr=nin}}). ''Một '''con''' người'' "a person" does not sound dehumanizing, but even literary, while ''một người'' sounds casual enough.
* The phrase ''con người'' is popularly employed as a philosophical trope or device to bring up discussions about what it means to be human as opposed to being an animal, even though it is not really semantically convincing given the fact that humans are, zoologically, animals, and there are non-animal things going with this classifier.

====Derived terms====
{{col3|vi|con dấu|con bạc|con thú|con vật|con nước}}

====See also====
* {{l|vi|cái}}

