cá thu.raw:
===Etymology===
The second element is from a {{bor|vi|tai|}} language. Compare {{cog|th|ทู}}.

Curiously, the Pacific saury, also known as the mackerel pike, is called {{m|vi|cá thu đao}} in Vietnamese, corresponding to {{m|zh|秋刀魚}} ([[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|[[thu]] [[đao]] [[ngư]]}}) in Chinese.

The ''thu'' elements in ''cá thu'' ("mackerel") and ''cá thu đao'' ("mackerel pike") are therefore seemingly unrelated, with the former being a Tai loan, while the latter is the Sino-Vietnamese reading of {{m|zh|秋}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=con|head=[[cá]] thu|[[个]]/[[𩵜]] + [[鰍]]/[[𩷊]]/[[𩹤]]}}

