cáy.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
{{rfe|vi|{{zh-ref|Baxter & Sagart (2014)}} considers it a reflex of the [[unprefixed]] form of {{der|vi|och|-}} {{och-l|蟹|tr={{IPAfont|*m-kˤreʔ}}|[[crab]]}} (B-S) (SV: {{m|vi|giải}}), but OC *''kr-'' regularly yields ‹s-›, in other cases ‹gi-›, ‹tr-›, and the rarer ‹ch-›, never retains *k-, in modern Vietnamese. 

Alternatively, cáy is from a post-OC but pre-MC layer which yields {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*ka:s}} > {{m|vi|cải}}, and {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*t-kɨəm}} > {{m|vi|gươm}} with velar initials.

Regardless, its ultimate origin is very likely {{bor|vi|sit}}; compare {{cog|sit-pro|*d-k(j)aːj||crab}}.}}

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=con|[[𧉝]], [[𧉄]], [[𧑂]], [[既]], [[𲿓]], [[𰳙]]}}

# [[fiddler crab]], {{vern|mangrove crab}}

====Derived terms====
