===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*t-kɔːj||[[horn]]}}. Cognate with {{cog|thm|-}} ''təkɔːj¹'' ("cow and buffalo horn"), {{cog|mkh-kat-pro|*tŋkɔɔj}} (whence {{cog|pac|tancoi||horn, antler}}), {{cog|km|កុយ||rhinoceros horn}}. The original meaning was probably "horn of a herbivore", while {{ncog|mkh-vie-pro|*k-rəŋ}} (> {{m|vi|sừng}}) was just "horn" in general.

The Viet-Muong languages no longer retain the meaning "horn of a herbivore" preserved in the other Vietic languages (like Thavung), Katuic and Khmer, but only "instrumental horn" (with the same semantic development as in English).

