[[File:Spondias cytherea - fruit (8750413284).jpg|thumb|{{lang|vi|[[quả]] '''cóc''' [[chín]]}}]]
Compare {{cog|mkh-kat-pro|*ʔakɔk}}, {{cog|kjg|-}} [Cuang] ''kok'', {{cog|th|กอก}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|vi|cốc}}

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|cls=[[cây]], [[trái]], [[quả]]|㭲}}

# [[species]] in the genus {{taxfmt|Spondias|genus}}, such as {{taxfmt|Spondias dulcis|species}}

===Etymology 4===
{{vi-etym-sino|覺|hv=n||giác}}.

This morpheme was extensively attested written with the phonogram {{ltc-l|谷|id=1}} in Nôm texts, however, it already fell into disuse for some time before the colonial period.

Because of the fact that it is already mostly obsolete before the wide adoption of the Latin script, in modern romanization of Nôm texts, the phonogram {{ltc-l|谷|id=1}} is also commonly transliterated as ''*cốc'', probably based on the Sino-Vietnamese reading {{m|vi|cốc}} of the grapheme; however, there is little direct evidence that this is closer to actual pronunciation of the word when it was in use. On the other hand, ''cóc'' is glossed as {{m|vi|biết||to know}} in ''Đại Nam quấc âm tự vị'' (1885), and the compound {{m|vi|cóc biết}} was translated as {{m|la|[[probe|probè]] [[intelligere]]||to understand well}} in ''Dictionarium Anamitico-Latinum'' (1838).

====Verb====
{{vi-verb|谷}}

# {{lb|vi|obsolete}} to be [[aware]] of; to [[know]]
#* ''Chỉ nam ngọc âm giải nghĩa'' (指南玉音解義)
#*: {{ux|vi|'''谷'''咍事世與令特收|tr='''Cóc''' hay sự thế dữ lành được thua.|To '''know''' the situation, good or bad, allows for one to be defeated.}}

