cất.raw:
===Etymology===
{{rfe|vi|The Austroasiatic root for "to arise" (whence {{ncog|km|កើត}}, {{ncog|kjg|-}} ''kəːt'' ("to be born")) is reminiscent of this Vietic form. This is probably coincidental though, Vietic has short vowel here, while the rest have long vowel, and semantically they are not that close once you look closer at the individual items. Compare 揭 (lit. to raise; to lift up; cf. OC: /*[k]at/, MC: /*kiæt̚/, Taishan: /kʰet̚³³/, Meixian: /kiat̚¹/, Xiamen: /kiɛt̚⁴/). For the sense "to clear; to relocate, to put back", compare to Chinese 收起 (lit. "to lift and put away")?}}
