cầy.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-pro|*cgəj}}. Cognate with {{cog|km|ឆ្កែ||dog}}, {{cog|bdq|sơke||wild boar}} and {{cog|ngt|-}} ''cakɛː'' ("dog").

{{cog|kha|skei||Indian muntjac, barking deer}} might be a loanword from a Sino-Tibetan language, cf. {{cog|my|ချေ||barking deer}}, {{cog|ksw|တခံ|တ'''ခံ'''|deer}}, {{cog|kac|chäkhji|chä'''khji'''|barking deer}}, and is not directly related to the other Austroasiatic items.

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|cls=con|猉}}

# [[civet]]; [[viverrid]] 
# {{short for|vi|thịt cầy||[[dog]] [[meat]]}}
#: {{uxi|vi|giả cầy|imitation dog meat}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col3|vi|cầy giông|cầy lỏn|cầy hương|cầy móc cua|giả cầy|cầy sấy|cầy cáo|cầy mực}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|vi|triết}}; {{l|vi|chồn}}

===Etymology 2===
Probably from the etymology above, compare {{cog|ms|pauh kijang||lit=muntjac's mango}}.

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|cls=cây|猉}}

# {{taxlink|Irvingia malayana|species}}
#: {{syn|vi|cốc|kơ nia}}

