===Etymology===
From {{compound|vi|cờ|t1=[[flag]]|ba|t2=[[three]]|que|t3=[[stick]]}}, literally means three-stick flag. "Ba que" is an idiom referring to a trick game played using three sticks and a leaf during French colonial rule, becoming synonymous with deceit and dishonesty.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|旗𠀧桂|cls=lá}}

# {{lb|vi|chiefly|communist Vietnamese|often|pejorative|slang|humorous}} the [[w:Flag_of_South_Vietnam|flag of the former Republic of Vietnam]]

====Usage notes====
The word is mockingly used for [[w:Flag_of_South_Vietnam|flag of the former Republic of Vietnam]], which is banned in Vietnam. It is used among the communist Vietnamese.

