dìa.raw:
===Etymology===
In general, in {{m|vi|Nẫu}} dialects, the monophthongs {{IPAfont|/e/}} and {{IPAfont|/ɛ/}} in mainstream dialects at final position shifted to {{IPAfont|/əː/}} (mainstream {{m|vi|quê}} vs. Nẫu {{m|vi|quơ}}, {{m|vi|để}} vs. {{m|vi|đở}}, {{m|vi|ghê}} vs. {{m|vi|gơ}}) and {{IPAfont|/iə/}} ({{m|vi|xe}} vs. {{m|vi|xia}}, {{m|vi|té}} vs. {{m|vi|tía}}, unless preceded by the glide {{IPAfont|/w/}}: {{m|vi|khoẻ}} vs. {{m|vi|phẻ}}) respectively. Yet in this case, Nẫu {{IPAfont|/iə/}} corresponds to mainstream {{IPAfont|/e/}}, not {{IPAfont|/ɛ/}}. Since the etymological vowel of this item was originally {{IPAfont|/e/}}, this iconic Nẫu form most likely indicates an irregular shift of {{IPAfont|/e > ɛ/}}.

