dù.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-dù.wav|a=Hanoi}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*duː||[[shelter]]}}. There are related words in many neighbouring languages. Compare {{cog|lo|ຍູ}} (as in {{m|lo|ຄັນຍູ}}) and {{cog|km|យូ}} (as in {{m|km|តាំងយូ}}). The distribution within both Tai languages and Austroasiatic does not indicate great time depth, so they might be borrowed from Vietnamese instead.

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|cls=[[cây]], [[cái]], [[chiếc]]|𢂎}}

# {{lb|vi|Southern Vietnam}} [[umbrella]]
#: {{syn|vi|ô}}
# [[parachute]]
#: {{uxi|vi|lính nhảy '''dù'''|paratrooper}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col3|vi|dù lượn <tr:paraglide>|nhảy dù <tr:to parachute>|ô dù <tr:umbrellas>|dù lọng}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|jra|yu|bor=1}}
* {{desc|blt|ꪏꪴ|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
Compare {{cog|ltc|-}} {{ltc-l|猶|still, yet|id=1}} (SV: {{l|vi|do}}).

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|vi|dẫu}}, {{l|vi|dầu}}

====Conjunction====
{{vi-conj|[[𠱋]], [[油]]}}

# {{lb|vi|literary|or|formal}} [[even if]], [[although]]

=====Usage notes=====
* ''Dù'' (and its related forms) is most often seen in written works and formal speech. In colloquial spoken Vietnamese, speakers would prefer to use {{m|vi|có}}...({{m|vi|thì}}) or some other structures instead to express what English speakers would use ''even if'' for. For example:
*: {{ux|vi|'''Có''' mệt '''thì''' vẫn phải làm cho xong đã chứ.|Even if you're tired, you still have (a task) you gotta complete.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col3|vi|dù cho|dù rằng|mặc dù <tr:although>|dù sao}}

