dấu ngã.raw:
===Etymology===
{{compound|vi|dấu|t1=mark|ngã|t2=to trip; to fall}} (from the fact that the word ''ngã'' has the tone written with a tilde).

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun}}

# {{lb|vi|typography}} [[tilde]] {{gloss|tone mark in Vietnamese}}
# {{lb|vi|colloquial}} creaky rising [[tone]]

====Usage notes====
This diacritic is a [[homoglyph]] of {{m|vi|dấu mềm}} or {{m|vi|dấu sóng}}, which refer to diacritical marks that resemble the tilde but do not carry the same meaning. The Portuguese {{m|pt|til|t=tilde}} was adopted by the original Vietnamese alphabet as {{m|vi|dấu sóng}}, which has fallen out of use.

The {{m|vi||dấu ngã}} diacritic itself derives from the Greek {{m|el|περισπωμένη|t=circumflex}}, which is a {{doublet|vi|dấu mũ|t1=circumflex|nocap=1}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|creaky rising tone}} {{vi-l|thanh ngã}}

====Coordinate terms====
