{{see citations|vi}}

====Derived terms====
{{col3|vi|em gái|em trai|anh em|chị em|anh chị em|em tam|đàn em|con em|trẻ em}}

===Pronoun===
{{vi-pronoun|[[㛪]], [[俺]], [[腌]]}}

# {{non-gloss|pronoun used to refer to any person (oneself, the addressee, or any third person) described by the noun ''em'' above}}
#: {{syn|vi|{{sense|second person}} [[thằng em]]|{{sense|third person}} em [[ấy]]|ẻm}}
#: {{uxi|vi|thằng em của '''em'''|'''my''' younger brother}}
## {{lb|vi|familiar}} {{non-gloss|pronoun used to refer to younger person of the same generation}}
## {{non-gloss|pronoun used to refer to younger siblings or cousins descended from an ancestor who is/was a younger sibling to one's own or one's spouse's}}
## {{lb|vi|formal}} {{non-gloss|pronoun used to refer to a [[child]] or a [[student]]}}
##: {{syn|vi|con}}
##: {{ux|vi|Viết một đoạn văn ngắn miêu tả một thứ bố '''em''' làm cho '''em'''.|Write a short essay describing something '''your''' father made for '''you'''.}}
# {{non-gloss|pronoun used to refer to the [[girl]] or [[woman]] in a [[romantic]] [[relationship]]}}
#: {{ant|vi|anh|eng|tôi|tui}}
#: {{ux|vi|Anh yêu '''em'''. / '''Em''' cũng yêu anh.|I love '''you'''. / '''I''' love you too.}}
#* {{quote-book|vi|translator=lw:vi:Hoàng Thúy Toàn|original=Я вас любил|title=Tôi yêu em|author=w:Alexander Pushkin|trans-title={{w|I Loved You (poem)|I Loved You}}|text=Tôi yêu '''em''' âm thầm, không hi vọng, / Lúc rụt rè, khi hậm hực lòng ghen, / Tôi yêu '''em''', yêu chân thành, đằm thắm, / Cầu '''em''' được người tình như tôi đã yêu '''em'''.|t=I loved '''you''', without words, without hope, / Sometimes I felt shy, sometimes I felt tortured with jealousy, / I loved '''you''', truly and deeply, / I pray '''you''' will find someone who loves '''you''' as much as I ever did.}}

====Usage notes====
* Textbooks tend to assume grade schoolers and middle schoolers to be young enough to be called {{m|vi|em|lit=little sibling}}, but high schoolers to be old enough to be called {{m|vi|anh||big brother}} and {{m|vi|chị||big sister}}.

