giuống.raw:
===Alternative forms===
* {{q|unetymological spelling}} {{l|vi|duống}}

===Etymology===
Probably from an affixed form of the root that gave rise to {{m|vi|xuống||to go downwards, to descend}}.

Attested in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651), a dictionary based chiefly on the Northern dialects, as {{m|mkh-mvi|giuống}}, glossed with {{ncog|la|descendo|deſcendo|to descend}}. Attested in ''Đại Nam quấc âm tự vị'' (1895), a dictionary based chiefly on the Southern dialects, as ''giuống'', glossed {{m|vi|[[nhấc]] [[ra]] [[khỏi]] [[bếp]]||to put down from the stove}}, noted as ''tiếng ít dùng'' ("uncommon word"), so most likely already obsolete or rare in the Southern dialects by then. 

Attested in ''Từ điển phương ngữ Huế'' ("A Dictionary of the Hue dialect(s)", 2017) with the unetymological spelling ''duống'', glossed as {{m|vi|[[nhấc]] ([[xuống]])||to put down}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Verb===
{{vi-verb|[[種]], [[降]]}}

# {{lb|vi|Central Vietnam|obsolete|_|in other dialects}} to [[put down]]
#: {{ux|vi|Con coi {{l|vi|trách}} cá cho {{l|vi|mạ}}, khi {{l|vi|mô}} thấy nước síp síp thì '''duống''' xuống nghe!|You go look after the pot of fish [that is being cooked] for me, once most of the water has evaporated, you must put the pot down from the fire.|ref=<ref>Trần, Ngọc Bảo (2017). "Từ Điển Phương Ngữ Huế".</ref>}}

===References===
