giải âm.raw:
{{wp}}
[[File:Bìa 'Thi kinh giải âm'.jpg|thumb|The book cover of Thi kinh giải âm 詩經解音 (1714).]]

===Etymology===
{{vi-etym-sino|解|to explain|音|Vietnamese}}. Âm is a clipping of the term quốc âm (國音; "national pronunciation"), which was used to refer to the Vietnamese language.

{{zh-x|因 念 寡陋 者 非 訓詁 不能 達 而 '''解音''' 則 訓詁 之 流 也。|Therefore, I pity those who are of little learning are not able to understand [texts] without xungu, and as for '''giải âm''', it is a branch of xungu.|CL-VN|collapsed=y}}

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun}}

# {{lb|vi|historical|translation}} a historical category of texts that aim to explain works written in [[Literary Chinese]] in the national pronunciation ([[Quốc âm]]).

====Usage notes====
* There is significant diversity within works called ''giải âm'' (even within a single text), with some coming fairly close to the modern concept of translation, while some are closer to annotations with "word-matching" between Literary Chinese and Vietnamese, with little to no regard to the structure or syntax of Vietnamese. On the contrary, some {{m|vi|giải nghĩa}}/{{m|vi|diễn nghĩa}} works focus on extracting as much meaning as possible from the source texts, with little to no regard to the structure and syntax of Literary Chinese.
*: '''16th century''', ''{{w|Truyền kỳ mạn lục}}'' (傳奇漫錄, "Casual Record of Transmitted Strange-Tales") by {{w|Nguyễn Dữ}}.
*: {{quote|zh|惟其剛之守|tr=Duy kì cương chi thủ.|Only keeping his steadfastness.}}
*:: '''16th century''', Nguyễn Thế Nghi's (attributed) ''Tân biên Truyền kỳ mạn lục tăng bổ giải âm tập chú'' (新編傳奇漫錄增補解音集註), ''giải âm''/"translation" of the ''{{w|Truyền kỳ mạn lục}}''.
*:: {{vi-ruby|盃所亘蒸𡨺|Bui thửa cứng chưng giữ.}}
* The "Vietnamese" line above closely matches the Chinese original on both character-by-character basis, and word order, although its readability as a "Vietnamese" sentence on its own (archaic vocabulary aside) is somewhat questionable. This example involves two common "translation devices" in ''giải âm'' texts: {{vi-link|thửa||所}}, commonly used to match with {{ltc-l|其|id=1}} and {{ltc-l|所}}, and {{vi-link|chưng||蒸}}, often matched with {{ltc-l|之}} and {{ltc-l|夫|id=1}}.

===See also===
* {{l|vi|giải nghĩa}}, a similar category of texts, with a stronger focus on "explaining the meaning"
* {{l|vi|diễn nghĩa}}
* {{l|vi|diễn ca}}, a similar category of texts, with a stronger focus on verse
* {{l|vi|ngạn giải}}, Korean equivalent 

{{c|vi|Vietnamese|Translation studies}}

