Unclear. The word is not Sino-Vietnamese and ⟨g/gh⟩ is also not a possible initial in Sino-Vietnamese proper, therefore the word might be either native, a vernacular Sinitic loan (either from a regional Sinitic language or is an early, pre-Middle Chinese loan), or a loan from another neighboring language. The Nôm character {{m|vi|棍}}, as with many other cases, is merely a character formed by phono-semantic matching.

The word might (but unlikely) be the second element in the placename {{m|vi|Sài Gòn}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=[[cây]], [[bông]]|棍}}

# [[ceiba]]
#: {{syn|vi|bông gòn}}
# {{lb|vi|by extension}} [[cotton]] [[pad]]

{{C|vi|Mallow family plants|Trees}}

