gần.raw:
===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|vi|gưn|q=North Central Vietnam}}
* {{alt|vi|gin|q=North Central Vietnam}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*t-kəɲ}}. Traditionally regarded as a non-[[Sino-Vietnamese]] reading of Chinese {{l|vi|近}} ([[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|cận}}).

There have been some proposals, including Miyake (2015) and Trần Trí Dõi (2016), that this term is not a loanword. The earliest layer of Sinitic loans in Vietic usually show the shift of {{IPAfont|*-r > *-n}} characteristic of the later stages of Old Chinese. However, there is no motivation for the shift of this {{IPAfont|*-n}} to {{IPAfont|*-ɲ}} (Rục kept Vietic ''*-n'' as is after all vowels). 

In any case, cognate with {{cog|mtq|-}} Bi {{m|mtq|khênh}}, {{cog|scb|-}} [Rục] ''təkiɲ¹'', {{cog|aem|kừnh}}. Attested in ''Phật thuyết đại báo phụ mẫu ân trọng kinh'' (佛說大報父母恩重經) as phonetic {{m|vi|斤}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|cân}})

