gỉ.raw:
===Alternative forms===
* {{l|vi|rỉ}}

===Etymology===
The spelling might be an unetymological spelling originated from the (inland) Northern region, where the ⟨r⟩-⟨gi⟩ merger took place (coastal dialects of southern Red River delta often still maintain the distinction). Compare {{cog|aem|-}} ''parɛh'' ("rusted, rusty").

Both senses listed below are related. Connection between "rust, rusted" and bodily discharges are amply attested crosslinguistically. Compare {{ncog|mtq|-}} Bi {{m|mtq|kếch||rusted, rusty}} (cognate of Vietnamese {{m|vi|cứt||shit}}), {{ncog|my|သံချေး||rust}}.

