===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*haːr}}, from {{inh|vi|aav-pro|*ɓaːr}} (or some variant presented by {{cog|mkh-pal-pro|*ləʔaːr}}, {{cog|kha|ar}}, {{cog|ncb|-}} [Nancowry] {{m|ncb|âṅ}}; Shorto reconstructed Pre-Mon-Khmer ''*biʔaar''). Cognate with {{cog|mtq|hal}}, {{cog|km|ពីរ}}, {{cog|bdq|'bar}}, {{cog|pac|bar}}, {{cog|kha|ar}}, {{cog|mnw|ၜါ}}, {{cog|sat|ᱵᱟᱨ}}.

Insertion of initial ''*h'' in Vietic can also be seen in {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*huːɲ||to kiss}} (> {{ncog|vi|hôn}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*heːt||finished}} (> {{ncog|vi|hết}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*hanʔ||he, she, it}} (> {{ncog|vi|hắn}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*hoːj||foul-smelling}} (> {{ncog|vi|hôi}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*tŋ-ʔaːm}} (> {{ncog|vi|hàm}}, Late Vietic), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*hɔːŋʔ||river, brook}}, {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*haːŋʔ||to open (mouth)}}.

====Numeral====
{{vi-pos|numeral|[[𠄩]], [[咍]], [[台]]}}

# {{cln|vi|cardinal numbers}} [[two]]

====Adjective====
{{vi-adj|[[𠄩]], [[咍]], [[台]]}}

# {{cln|vi|ordinal numbers}} {{lb|vi|southern Vietnam|of a sibling}} [[eldest or elder]]; [[firstborn]]
#: {{syn|vi|cả}}
#: {{uxi|vi|anh/chị '''hai'''|eldest brother/sister}}
#: {{uxi|vi|bác '''hai'''|eldest brother/sister of one's parent}}

