hun.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
Typical Central and Southern Vietnamese retention of medial ''*u'', which often developed into ‹ô› (or ‹o›) in Northern dialects; later strengthened with the use of "slang" to avoid awkward situations. Compare {{m|vi|rún}} vs. {{m|vi|rốn}}, {{m|vi|thúi}} vs. {{m|vi|thối}}.

====Verb====
{{vi-verb|[[㖧]]}}

# {{alternative form of|vi|hôn||to kiss|from=central Vietnam|from2=southern Vietnam}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The Northern form with {{IPAfont|[o]}} is pretty much never used in daily speech by speakers of Central and Southern dialects, although they might choose to use it in formal writing.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|vi|thơm}}, {{l|vi|hôn}}, {{l|vi|chu}}, {{l|vi|chụt}}, {{l|vi|mi}}

===Etymology 2===
{{vi-etym-sino|熏||hv=n|huân}}.

====Verb====
{{vi-verb|[[焝]], [[熏]], [[燻]]}}

# to [[smoke]] (to preserve or prepare (food) for consumption by treating with smoke)

