* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-hàm.wav|a=Hanoi}}

===Etymology 1===
From Late Proto-Vietic ''*-haːm'', from {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*tŋ-ʔaːm}}, from {{inh|vi|aav-pro|*tʔaːm||molar tooth}}. Cognate with {{cog|tou|-}} [Cuối Chăm] ''hɐːm²'', {{cog|scb|-}} [Rục] ''təŋʔaːm¹'', {{cog|hal|tơ'am||molar tooth}}, {{cog|pac|tang-am||back teeth; bottom molars}}, {{cog|dnu|-}} ''ʔɑm¹'', {{cog|kha|tyng-am||jawbone}}.

Insertion of initial ''*h'' in Vietic can also be seen in {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*huːɲ||to kiss}} (> {{ncog|vi|hôn}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*heːt||finished}} (> {{ncog|vi|hết}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*hanʔ||he, she, it}} (> {{ncog|vi|hắn}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*haːr||two}} (> {{ncog|vi|hai}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*hoːj||foul-smelling}} (> {{ncog|vi|hôi}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*hɔːŋʔ||river, brook}}, {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*haːŋʔ||to open (mouth)}}.

Not derived from {{ncog|zh|-}} {{ltc-l|頷|id=2}}, ''OC'' {{IPAfont|*[ɢ]ˤ[ə]mʔ}} (B-S), in spite of the similar SV reading {{m|vi|hạm}}.

