===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-hôn.wav|a=Hanoi}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*huːɲ}}, from {{inh|vi|mkh-pro|*ɟʔuuɲ|*ɟʔuuɲ ~ *ɟhuuɲ}} (Shorto). Compare Central and Southern Vietnamese {{m|vi|hun}}, {{cog|mkh-kat-pro|*huuɲ ~ *huoɲ||to smell, to sniff}} (whence {{cog|kdt|-}} ''huːɲ'' ("to smell, to sniff") and {{cog|pac|hunh||to kiss}}), {{cog|kns|-}} ''ʔɔɲ'' ("to smell, to sniff, to kiss").

Insertion of initial ''*h'' in Vietic can also be seen in {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*tŋ-ʔaːm||jaw}} (> {{ncog|vi|hàm}}, Late Vietic), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*heːt||finished}} (> {{ncog|vi|hết}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*hanʔ||he, she, it}} (> {{ncog|vi|hắn}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*haːr||two}} (> {{ncog|vi|hai}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*hoːj||foul-smelling}} (> {{ncog|vi|hôi}}), {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*hɔːŋʔ||river, brook}}, {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*haːŋʔ||to open (mouth)}}.

