hơn.raw:
===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-pro|*hən}} ~ {{m|mkh-pro|*həən||to grow, to increase}} (Shorto 2006, #1219); cognate with {{cog|aem|-}} ''hɨən'' ("more than; to defeat, to win against"), {{cog|pac|hon||grown}}, {{cog|bdq|hon||to grow}}, Plang [La Gang] ''hɔ́n'', and {{cog|kha|byrhien||(people) in large numbers}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-hơn.wav|a=Hanoi}}

===Adverb===
{{vi-adv|欣}}

# [[more]], [[-er]], to a greater degree or extent
#: {{uxi|vi|to '''hơn'''|bigg'''er'''}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''hơn''' một năm|'''more''' than a year}}
#: {{ux|vi|Tôi thích tiếng Việt '''hơn''' tiếng Anh.|I like Vietnamese '''more''' than English.}}
#: {{uxi|vi|không '''hơn''' không kém|neither '''more''' nore less}}

====Usage notes====
The word “[[than]]”, which English requires in front of the standard after a comparative degree, is not translated:
: {{uxi|vi|đẹp '''hơn''' cái này|'''more''' beautiful [than] this one}}

===Adjective===
{{vi-adj|欣}}

# [[better]]
#: {{ux|vi|Có '''hơn''' nó chỗ nào đâu mà chém kinh thế?|You're not '''better''' than him/her at anything, stop shit talking.}}

====Derived terms====
{{col|vi|hơn cả|hơn hết|hơn nữa|không hơn không kém|hơn thua}}

===Anagrams===
