#: {{ux|vi|Bây giờ mấy giờ rồi '''hở''' chị?|Excuse me, what time is it?}}

=====Usage notes=====
<!--  The interrogative particle ''hở'' is used immediately before a [[personal pronoun]] at the end of a question to make the question more polite. It is similar to the English "ma'am", "sir" or "excuse me".
This is actually a very widespread phenomenon that is applied not only to hở but to most if not all final particles (nha cô, nhỉ bác, à chị, etc.). And well it's not really polite, but more like for emphasis or topic marking, see the example I added, no way "hở mày" is polite. -->
* Very often, ''hở'' is used in combination with {{m|vi|ơi}}.
:: {{uxi|vi|Bác <u>ơi</u>, bác có biết đến khách sạn đi đường nào không '''hở''' bác?|Excuse me sir! Do you know the way to the hotel?}}

