{{rfe|vi|In many Vietic and Austroasiatic languages (such as Khmer), velar stop is often non-phonemically aspirated before sonorants (cf. Kha Phong ''kʰalaː¹'' ("noon") < {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*k-laː}}), so the Proto-Vietic form can be obtained after simple metathesis: pre-Proto-Vietic ''*k-laːʔ'' {{IPAfont|[kʰ(ə)laːʔ]}} > Proto-Vietic ''*k-haːlʔ''. Compare also the proto-forms of {{m|vi|gió}} and {{m|vi|khói}}, which might be related to each other through the same exact pattern of metathesis.}}

From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*kʰaːlʔ|*k-haːlʔ / *kʰaːlʔ}}, from {{inh|vi|aav-pro|*kla(ː)ʔ}}. Cognate with {{cog|km|ខ្លា}}, {{cog|bdq|kla}}, {{cog|kha|khla}}, {{cog|mnw|ကၠ}}. {{doublet|vi|hổ}}.

