khách hàng.raw:
===Etymology===
From {{com|vi|khách|hàng|t1=guest; customer; client|t2=goods}}. ''khách'' by itself usually implies that the person physically goes to a shop or store, but ''khách hàng'' has a broader connotation, as in a client who uses any service that doesn't necessarily require them to physically go anywhere, such as Internet service, telephone service, or work on commission. Incidentally, the {{m|vi|hàng||goods}} in this word and the {{m|vi|hành||to go}} in {{m|vi|hành khách||passenger}} both derive from {{cog|zh|行}}, making the Nom spelling of this and the Sino-Vietnamese spelling of {{m|vi|hành khách}} accidental anagrams.

