===Particle===
{{head|vi|particle}}

# {{n-g|Used to form polar questions, placed at the end of a question}}
#: {{ux|vi|Anh ấy đang chạy đúng/phải không?|He is running, '''isn't''' he?}}
#: {{ux|vi|Bạn chưa làm phải '''không'''?|You haven't done anything, '''have''' you?}}
#: {{ux|vi|Có ai ở nhà '''không''' (ạ)?|Anybody home?}}
#: {{ux|vi|Đúng '''không'''?|'''Is''' that true?}}
# {{n-g|Used as an answer of refutation to a polar question}}: [[no]]
#: {{ux|vi|Bạn có phải là người Anh không? '''Không''', tôi không/chả phải (là người Anh).|Are you British? '''No''', I'm not.}}

====Usage notes====
{{box-top|Grammar}}
* The [[interrogative]] expression ''có'' … ''không'' forms in most cases a [[yes-no question]] and encircles the [[verbal]] or [[adjectival]] [[predicate]]. ''Có'' is placed in front of the verb or adjective, and ''không'' comes at the end of the sentence. Such questions are "open" questions in the sense that there is no expectation of the behalf of the speaker that the answer will be "yes" or "no". The word order is: [[subject]] + ''có'' + predicate + ''không''? In [[informal]] communication, ''có'' can be omitted. Such yes-no questions regularly permit the use of the repetition of ''có'' as an affirmative answer form.
*: {{ux|vi|A: [[mấy|Mấy]] [[đứa]] [[bạn]] anh (có) [[hay]] đi [[phượt]] '''[[không]]'''?<br>B: Có.|A: Do your friends often go on road trips on motorbikes?<br>B: Yes.}}
*: {{ux|vi|A: Anh (có) [[khoẻ]] '''không'''?<br>B: Có.|A: How are you?<br>B: Good.}}
* The interrogative expression ''có phải'' … ''không'' also forms a yes-no question and encircles the [[nominal]] predicate and

