kẹo cu đơ.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
The creator, Đinh Vy, used to sell these candies to locals for two coins. He was therefore nicknamed "Cu Hai" (with [[hai|Hai]] meaning two). Some French officers, who often visited to buy the candy, translated the latter part of the name into the French word "[[deux|Deux]]" (which reads "đơ" in Vietnamese). This new latter part stuck around and gave rise to the name "Cu Đơ", replacing the original "Cu Hai".<ref>https://vnexpress.net/nguon-goc-ten-goi-keo-cu-do-4515505.html</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=cái}}

# kind of [[candy]] made from a mixture of [[peanut]]s, sliced [[ginger]] and [[glutinous rice]] [[malt]] [[syrup]], served between two pieces of [[rice cracker|rice crackers]].

