làm.raw:
===Alternative forms===
* {{q|Quảng Nam, Quảng Ngãi}} {{l|vi|lồm}}

===Etymology===
A {{doublet|vi|là|t1=to [[be]]; to [[work]]|nocap=1}}; see there for more. The {{IPAfont|-m}} "suffix" is of unknown function and origin. This is an innovation in Vietnamese, not found in Mường and other Vietic languages.

For the semantic relation, compare also {{ncog|zh|為|tr=vi||to [[do]]; to [[be]]}}.

Most prepositions in Vietnamese were originally verbs: {{m|vi|ở||to stay; at, in}}, {{m|vi|đến||to come; to}}, {{m|vi|tới||to arrive; to}}, {{m|vi|lên||to go up; onto}}, {{m|vi|vào||to enter; in, into}}, {{m|vi|theo||to follow; according to}}, {{m|vi|về||to return; about}}, {{m|vi|cho||to give; for}}.

The Nôm character {{vi-l|𫜵}} was unified in Unicode with {{l|vi|爫|t=top form of Kangxi radical #87}} up until the version 14.0 (2021). See the entry for details.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{IPA|vi|[lɑm˧˩]|a=Quảng Nam}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-làm.wav|a=Hanoi}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-làm.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Verb===
