* There are multiple words for villages and it is not always clear what the differences are, although it does seem to be a matter of regional and ethnic preference. Northern villages of the ethnically Vietnamese are either {{m|vi|làng}} or {{m|vi|thôn}}. Highlanders' villages are {{m|vi|bản}}, and Central Highland villages are {{m|vi|buôn}}. Southern villages of the ethnically Vietnamese tend to be {{m|vi|ấp}}, while Khmer villages are {{m|vi|sóc}}.

