lên.raw:
===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*leːɲ}}, from {{inh|vi|mkh-pro|*luŋ|*luŋ ~ *luəŋ ~ *ləŋ|above, on}} (reconstruction in Shorto, 2006); related to {{m|vi|trên}}. Cognate with {{cog|mtq|liênh}}, {{cog|scb|-}} [Rục] ''liːŋ¹'', {{cog|sxm|-}} ''liɲ'' ("to go up; on"), {{cog|km|ឡើង}}, {{cog|sza|-}} ''leŋ'' ("upwards, upstream"), {{cog|jun|-}} ''aliŋ-ta'' ("above, from above, on; up, upon"), {{cog|kfq|-}} ''liɲ'' ("up, above").

Note that the reconstruction by Ferlus (2007) is inaccurate at Proto-Vietic level. The fronting of final {{IPAfont|*-ŋ}} to {{IPAfont|*-ɲ}} after front vowels only occured at Common Viet-Muong stage, not Proto-Vietic proper, hence non-Viet-Muong languages (like Rục) keep final {{IPAfont|*-ŋ}} intact. The reconstruction {{IPAfont|*leːɲ}} is thus accurate for the Common Viet-Muong stage, but the Proto-Vietic form can be mended to {{IPAfont|*leːŋ}} instead. 

For some other examples of Common Viet-Muong fronting of {{IPAfont|*-ŋ}} after front vowels, compare Viet. {{m|vi|đến}} vs. Cuối Chăm ''teːŋ³'', Viet. {{m|vi|cù lần}} vs. Cuối Chăm ''kuː¹ liŋ¹'', Viet. {{m|vi|chân}} vs. Rục ''ciːŋ²''.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-lên.wav|a=Hanoi}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-lên.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Verb===
{{vi-verb|[[蓮]], [[連]], [[𨑗]], [[𨕭]], [[𨖲]], [[𫧧]], [[𬨠]], [[𬨺]]}}

# to [[go up]], [[come up]], [[rise]]
# to be or [[reach]] a certain age
# to get on (a {{l|en|vehicle}})
#: {{coi|vi|thẻ '''lên''' máy bay|'''boarding''' pass}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''lên''' xe|to '''get on/in''' the car}}
# to go to (a more developed area)
#: {{uxi|vi|'''lên''' thành phố|to '''go''' to the city}}
# {{lb|vi|of a machine}} to be [[activate]]d
