lòng lang dạ sói.raw:
===Etymology===
Both ''lòng lang'' and ''dạ sói'' mean “wolf’s heart”, or more literally, “wolf’s intestines, wolf’s stomach”, and they are combined into a reduplication for emphasis, which is found in some Vietnamese fossil compounds (see also {{m|vi|rừng rú}}, {{m|vi|xe cộ}}, etc.). There are also literary phrases such as {{m|vi|[[loài]] lang [[sói]]||{{l|en|[[ruthless]] [[beast]]s}}|lit=wolf {{l|en|kind}}}}. {{m|vi|lang||[[wolf]]}} is a {{vi-etym-sino|狼}}.

