lăm.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-lăm.wav|a=Hanoi}}

===Etymology 1===
Alteration of {{m|vi|năm||five}} after {{m|vi|mười||ten}} (realized as {{m|vi|mươi}} due to tonal shift when fused with a preceding syllable; compare {{m|vi|bao '''nhiêu'''}}), which historically derives from {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*maːl}}, whence also {{cog|mtq|mườl}}. The historically final /l/ in {{m|vi|mười}}/{{m|vi|mươi}} causes the initial /n/ of {{m|vi|năm}} to assimilate to /l/, producing {{m|vi|mười '''lăm'''}}, {{m|vi|hai mươi '''lăm'''}}, {{m|vi|ba mươi '''lăm'''}}, ..., and {{m|vi|chín mươi '''lăm'''}}. Compare {{cog|ko|월'''남'''}} with similar sound change.

Sometimes thought to be a phonetic strategy to distinguish {{m|vi|năm||five}} from the homophonous {{m|vi|năm||year}}, as in {{m|vi|mười '''lăm'''||ten and '''five''' → fifteen}} and {{m|vi|mười '''năm'''||ten '''years'''}}; however, this is only a coincidence, because the homophonous {{m|vi|năm||year}} did not undergo consonant assimilation because {{m|vi|mười '''năm'''}} contains a word boundary, whereas {{m|vi|mười '''lăm'''}} is a fused compound referring to a numeral.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|vi|nhăm|q1=Northern Vietnam}}

====Numeral====
{{vi-pos|numeral|𠄻}}

# {{alternative form of|vi|năm|t=five|from=Post-[[mười]]/[[mươi]] [[allomorph]]ic|}}
#: ''mười '''lăm'''''
#:: fifteen
#: ''hai (mươi) '''lăm'''''
#:: twenty-five

=====Usage notes=====
* The variant {{m|vi|nhăm}} is used in Northern Vietnam in numbers greater than 20. See also {{m|vi|nói ngọng}}.

===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
{{vi-verb}}

