|original= {{lang|zh|《[[w:zh:s:黃鶴樓 (崔顥)|黃鶴樓]]》}}|by= w:zh:崔顥<t:{{w|Cui Hao (poet)|Cui Hao}}>|origlang= lzh
|origyear= 8th century {{CE}}|newversion= English translation from|year2= 2009|translator2= Peter Harris|title2= Three Hundred Tang Poems|page2= 39
|text= Hạc vàng ai cưỡi đi đâu?<br>Mà đây Hoàng Hạc riêng '''lầu''' còn trơ!
|translation= Long ago someone rode away on a yellow crane;<br>All that’s left here, pointlessly, is Yellow Crane '''Tower'''.
|origtext= zh:昔人已乘黃鶴去，<br>此地空餘黃鶴'''樓'''。}}
#* {{quote-book|vi|year= 1987|chapter=Tại {{lw|vi|Hoàng Hạc lâu|lầu Hoàng Hạc}} tiễn {{lw|vi|Mạnh Hạo Nhiên}} đi Quảng Lăng|translator=w:vi:Ngô Tất Tố|title=Thơ Đường|volume=2|trans-title=Tang Poetry
|original= {{lang|zh|《[[w:zh:s:黃鶴樓送孟浩然之廣陵|黃鶴樓送孟浩然之廣陵]]》}}|by= w:zh:李白<t:{{w|Li Bai}}>|origyear= 8th century {{CE}}|origlang= lzh
|newversion= English translation from|title2= Classical Chinese Poems in English|year2= 2010|chapter2= At the Yellow Crane Tower to Bid Meng Haoran Bon Voyage [to Guangling]|translator2= w:zh:黃宏發<t:{{w|Andrew Wong (politician)|Andrew Wong}}>|chapterurl2= https://chinesepoemsinenglish.blogspot.com/2010/07/li-bai-at-yellow-crane-tower-to-bid.html
|text= Bạn từ '''lầu''' Hạc lên đường<br>Giữa mùa hoa khói châu Dương xuôi dòng
|translation= At the Yellow Crane '''Tower''', my friend, to the west you said goodbye;<br>In this misty, flowery glorious spring, downstream for Yangzhou you ply.
|origtext= zh:故人西辭黃鶴'''樓'''，<br>煙花三月下揚州。}}
# {{lb|vi|architecture|chiefly|southern Vietnam}} [[floor]]/[[storey]] (except the [[ground floor]]/storey), 
#: {{syn|vi|tầng}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''lầu''' 2|floor one level above the ground floor; i.e. 2nd '''floor''' {{q|{{w|US}}}}}}
#: {{uxi|vi|nhà '''lầu'''|multi-storey house|lit= '''storey'''ed house}}
#: {{uxi|vi|nhảy '''lầu''' tự tử|to jump off a [high] '''floor''' to kill oneself}}
# {{lb|vi|architecture|chiefly|southern Vietnam|rare|proscribed}} [[floor]]/[[storey]] (including the [[ground floor]]/storey)
#: {{syn|vi|tầng}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''lầu''' trệt|ground floor}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''lầu''' 1|floor one level above the ground floor; i.e. 1st '''floor''' {{q|{{w|Europe}}}}}}
#* {{quote-web|vi|work= Bệnh Viện FV|date= 4 May 2021
|title= FV Tiếp Tục Hưởng Ứng Ngày Vệ Sinh Tay Thế Giới|titleurl= https://www.fvhospital.com/tin-tuc/fv-tiep-tuc-huong-ung-ngay-ve-sinh-tay-the-gioi/
|newversion= English version in|date2= 4 May 2021|type2= journal|work2= FV Hospital
|title2= FV Continues To Respond To World Hand Hygiene Day|titleurl2= https://www.fvhospital.com/news/fv-continues-to-respond-to-world-hand-hygiene-day/
|text= Ngoài ra, Biệt đội Kiểm soát Nhiễm khuẩn (KSNK) của bệnh viện cũng tổ chức quầy thông tin tại '''lầu''' trệt, để hướng dẫn mọi người thực hiện rửa tay đúng cách.
|translation= The Hospital’s Infection Control Unit will also organise an information counter on the ground '''floor''' to guide people in how to correctly wash their hands.}}

====Usage notes====
In southern and south-central Vietnamese, all floors are called '''lầu''' (as a result, {{m|vi||lầu trệt|ground floor}} is actually attested), although {{w|Linguistic prescription|prescriptivists}} proscribe such usage and advocate for using '''lầu''' to denote only floors above the ground floor.<ref name = "thingvn">{{cite-web|vi|work= VN Thing: Nội thất & Xây dựng|date= 24 May 2021|origdate= 7 March 2020|title= Tầng trệt là gì?|titleurl= https://thing.vn/tang-tret-la-gi}}</ref><ref name = "nganthinh">{{cite-web|vi|work= Xây Dựng Ngân Thịnh|trans-work= Ngân Thịnh Design and Build|date= 11 January 2023|title= Tầng trệt là gì? Cách phân biệt tầng và lầu|titleurl= https://xaydungnganthinh.com/tang-tret-la-gi}}</ref> 

By contrast, in northern and north-central Vietnamese, floors are called {{m|vi|tầng}}, the ground floor is called {{m|vi||tầng trệt}} or numbered as {{m|vi||tầng 1}},<ref name = "thingvn"/><ref name = "nganthinh"/> and {{m|vi||tầng 0}} technically refers to a [[crawl space]].

In central Vietnamese, floors are either called '''lầu''' or {{m|vi|tầng}}.<ref name = "thingvn"/><ref name = "nganthinh"/>

