lằng.raw:
===Alternative forms===
* {{l|vi|lằn}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*-laŋ||bluebottle fly}}, from {{der|vi|och|-}} {{och-l|蠅|tr={{IPAfont|*m-rəŋ}}|[[housefly]]}} (B-S) (SV: {{m|vi|dăng}}). {{cog|scb|-}} [Rục] cognate ''məlaŋ¹'' suggests the presence of pre-syllable ''*m-'' in Proto-Vietic.

This is an example of a Sinitic loanword borrowed at the stage when the shift {{IPAfont|*m-r- > *m-l-}}<ref>{{cite-book|author1= {{w|William H. Baxter|Baxter, William H.}}|author2= {{w|Laurent Sagart|Sagart, Laurent}}|year= 2014|title= Old Chinese:A New Reconstruction|page= 122}}</ref> already happened. Compare {{m|vi|lẽ||reason}} < {{ncog|mkh-mvi|mlẽ}}, from {{ncog|zh|理}} (phonetic {{och-l|里|tr={{IPAfont|*m(ə).rəʔ}}}}).

