mai gầm.raw:
===Etymology===
The element ''mai'' is either inherited from {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|-}}, or, more likely, borrowed from another {{bor|vi|aav}} language. In any case, cognate with {{cog|mtq|-}} Bi {{m|vi|màl||banded krait}} and {{cog|mkh-khm-pro|*maːr||snake}} (whence {{cog|pnx|-}} ''maːr'' ("snake")). 

Since cognates of this word in other Austroasiatic branches mean "to crawl" (cf. {{cog|pac|môr}}), and only developed the meaning of "snake" in Vietic and Khmuic, if Vietnamese ''mai'' was borrowed and not inherited, it could only have had borrowed from a fellow Vietic language (such as a Muong lect) or from Khmuic.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=con|head=mai [[gầm]]}}

