muông.raw:
===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*t-mɔːŋ||[[civet]]}}. Compare {{cog|zng|-}} ''muaŋ⁶'' ("civet").

Aside from a few compounds, the word is no longer used in Vietnamese. It also seems to once function as a classifier for a few animals, as attested in {{m|mkh-mvi|muông [[ſư tử]]||a lion}} (in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'') and {{m|mkh-mvi|[[獴]][[麟]]|tr=muông lân||a female of the qilin}} (in the ''Thi kinh giải âm'', 詩經解音, a {{m|vi|giải âm}} quasi-translation of the ''Shijing'').

The undiphthongized form of this word might be preserved in the name of {{lw|vi|hang Con Moong|Con Moong cave}}, located in northern Thanh Hoá.

