máy.raw:
===Etymology===
Cognate with {{cog|mtq|-}} Bi {{m|mtq|bẳl}} (as in {{m|vi|bẳl măt||to blink}}, equivalent to Vietnamese {{m|vi|máy mắt}}).

Originally a verb meaning "to move, to touch". This meaning can still be seen in the [[Appendix:Vietnamese reduplication#t- reduplication|''t-'' reduplicative]] {{m|vi|táy máy}} and the [[Appendix:Vietnamese reduplication#-âp reduplication|''-âp'' reduplicative]] {{m|vi|mấp máy}}, as well as some compounds like {{m|vi|mó máy}} and the aforementioned {{m|vi|máy mắt}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-máy.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Verb===
{{vi-verb|[[𢵯]], [[𣛠]], [[𠃅]]}}

# {{lb|vi|no longer used in isolation}} to [[move]] around
# {{lb|vi|no longer used in isolation}} to [[touch]] and [[feel]]
#* {{quote-book|vi|year=1914|title=南國方言俗語備錄<tr:Nam quốc phương ngôn tục ngữ bị lục><t:Records of the Southern Nation's regional adages and common sayings>|url=https://lib.nomfoundation.org/collection/1/volume/74/page/13|page=13b|passage=𠁀𧍆𧍆'''𢵯'''𠁀𧑂𧑂陶|tr=Đời cua cua '''máy''', đời cáy cáy đào.|t=A big crab's life just '''fiddling''' with its surroundings, a small crab's life is just digging.}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|[[𢵯]], [[𣛠]], [[𠃅]]|cls=[[cái]], [[cỗ]], [[bộ]]}}

# {{lb|vi|obsolete}} [[effect]]; [[mechanism]]
#* {{RQ:Nguyen Gia Thieu Cung oan ngam khuc|edition=Phú Văn đường tàng (富文堂藏), printed in 1866|passage=箕世局如印聀梦</br>'''𠃅'''玄微𨷑㨂坤量|transliteration=Kìa thế cục như in giấc mộng,</br>'''Máy''' huyền vi mở đóng khôn lường.|translation=See, how my situation is as if it's a dream,</br>The mysterious '''way that things move''', constantly changing and unpredictable.}}
# [[machine]]
# [[engine]]
# [[internal combustion engine]]
# {{lb|vi|colloquial}} [[phone]], [[mobile phone]]
#: {{uxi|vi|nhấc '''máy'''|to pick up the '''phone'''}}

====Usage notes====
* The classifier {{m|vi|cỗ||< a set of dishes in a feast}} seems to be mostly used in translation and the phrase ''cỗ máy'' appears to be quite lexicalized to the extent that its usage resembles that of a compound.

