mí.raw:
===Etymology===
Ferlus reconstructed {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*k-piːl}} ~ {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*ɓiːlʔ||[[eyelid]]}}. This is a curious etymology. 

The potential {{cog|mtq|-}} Bi cognate {{m|mtq|pèl}} is attested in ''Từ điển Mường-Việt'' (2002), having an A tone and pointing to a plain stop, while the Vietnamese word has a nasal, which points to the implosive {{IPAfont|*ɓ}}, and a B tone. The various clearly cognate forms are attested in ''Ngữ âm tiếng Mường qua các phương ngôn'' (1982), with both forms showing tone A (akin to Mường Bi) and tone B (akin to Vietnamese). {{cog|tou|-}} [Cuối Chăm] ''biːl³'' agrees with Vietnamese in both initial and tone.

