mươi.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-mươi.wav|a=Hanoi}}

===Etymology 1===
Nominalized from {{m|vi|mười||ten}}, due to the practice of combining single numerals with the decade numeral {{m|vi|mười}} to form decade numerals other than {{m|vi|mười}} itself. The tonal shift was triggered by the preceding numeral and is now fossilized. Compare {{m|vi|bao '''nhiêu'''||how '''many'''}} (← {{m|vi|nhiều}}), the dialectal {{m|vi|bao '''lăm'''||how '''many'''}} (← {{m|vi|lắm}}), the obsolete {{m|vi|bao '''dai'''||how '''long'''}} (← {{m|vi|dài}}), and {{m|vi|nước '''miếng'''||'''mouth''' fluid; saliva}} (← {{m|vi|miệng}}).

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|[[邁]], [[𨒒]], [[𱑕]], [[辻]], [[𨑮]]}}

# {{lb|vi|only used after numerals or determiners}} [[ten]]
#: {{syn|vi|chục}}
#: {{uxi|vi|tám '''mươi'''|“eight '''tens'''” → “eighty”}}
#: {{uxi|vi|tuổi vài '''mươi'''|“age of a few '''tens'''” → “in one's twenties”}}
#: {{uxi|vi|vài '''mươi''' năm nữa|“in a few '''tens''' of years” → “in a few decades”}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Unlike {{m|vi|một '''chục'''||a '''ten'''}}, {{m|vi|một '''mươi'''||a '''ten''' → ten}} is not considered correct, although theoretically possible. It is sometimes used humorously however.
* These two points are applied only when ''mươi'' is followed by another numeral:
** ''Mươi'' is very often elided in colloquial speech, so {{m|vi|[[ba]] [[mốt]]||thirty-one}} and {{m|vi|[[tám]] [[sáu]]||eighty-six}} are generally more common than the full forms {{m|vi|[[ba]] "mươi" [[mốt]]}} and {{m|vi|[[tám]] "mươi" [[sáu]]}} in the daily language.
** For {{m|vi|hai mươi||twenty}} and {{m|vi|ba mươi||thirty}} specifically, the contracted forms {{m|vi|hăm}} and {{m|vi|băm}}, where ''mươi'' is reduced to {{IPAfont|/m/}}, are also common, therefore {{m|vi|[[hăm]] [[bảy]]||twenty-seven}}, {{m|vi|[[băm]] [[ba]]||thirty-three}}. Note that this only happens when followed by another numeral.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|vi|đôi mươi}}
* {{l|vi|mười mươi}}

===Etymology 2===
From Etymology 1, due to the dropping of preceding determiners in {{m|vi|'''vài''' mươi||'''a few''' tens}} and {{m|vi|'''mấy''' mươi||'''some''' tens}}, turning {{m|vi|mươi}} into a determiner.

