mạt cưa mướp đắng.raw:
{{was fwotd|vi|2025|September|25}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|vi|mướp đắng mạt cưa}}

===Etymology===
{{com+|vi|mạt cưa|t1=[[sawdust]]|mướp đắng|t2=[[bitter melon]]}}, from a folktale about how two fraudulent merchants - one selling [[sawdust]] as [[bran]] and another selling [[bitter melon]]s as [[cucumber]]s - ended up defrauded by one another.

Earliest extant attestation of this figure of speech is in the poem "Tương phùng (Chance Meeting)" in ''{{lw|vi|Hồng Đức quốc âm thi tập}} (Collection of poems in our nation's language in the {{w|Lê Thánh Tông|Hồng Đức era}})'', vol. 3, folio 58b {{defdate|15th century {{CE}}}}:
* {{uxi|vi|'''𦲾䔲'''𠸦埃𢬭'''末鋸'''|tr='''Mướp đắng''' khen ai đổi '''mạt cưa'''.|Praiseworthy is anyone who trades '''sawdust''' for '''bittermelon'''.}}

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|head=[[mạt cưa]] [[mướp đắng]]}}

# {{lb|vi|idiomatic}} [[deceiver]], swindler, fraudster, scammer
#* {{RQ:Nguyen Du TK 1866|lines=811–812|passage=情期拯限麻年</br>'''𩈘鋸𦲾䔲'''堆邊𱥺坊|transliteration=Tình cờ chẳng hẹn mà nên,<br>'''Mạt cưa mướp đắng''' đôi bên một phường.|translation=They got acquainted with each other by chance without premeditation.<br>What a couple, '''a swindler and a scammer''', two of the same ilk!}}
#* {{quote-book|vi|author= Nguyễn Văn Thịnh|year= 2011|title= Thời Bi Tráng|trans-title= A Tragic and Majestic Time
|chapter= 8|chapterurl= https://sachhiem.net/NGVTHINH/NguyenvThinh_TBTg.php
|text= Cùng phường '''mạt cưa mướp đắng''' cả! – Ông giáo cười khẩy:… Dù Diều hâu hay Bồ câu, đều phải vì nước Mỹ, lợi thì vơ vào, bất lợi thì phải nhả ra thôi!
|translation= "They're all '''deceivers and fraudsters'''!" [[snicker|Snicker]]ed the Professor: "Whether hawks or doves, they must all act in the United States' interests; if they could profit, they'd hog everything; if they could not profit, they'd spit it all out!"}}

