* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-mọi.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Etymology 1===
{{vi-etym-sino|每|every, each|hv=n|mỗi}}. {{doublet|vi|mỗi}}.

Attested as {{m|mkh-mvi|mọi}} in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651).

====Determiner====
{{vi-determ|[[每]]}} 

# [[all]]
#: {{ux|vi|Một người vì '''mọi''' người! '''Mọi''' người vì một người!|One for all! All for one!}}

=====Usage notes=====
{{m|vi|mỗi|Mỗi}} (SV) and ''mọi'' (non-SV) are doublets from the same Chinese etymon, but their meanings differ: ''mỗi'' emphasises individuality (“each”), while ''mọi'' emphasises collectivity (“every”).

=====Derived terms=====
{{col|vi|mọi người|mọi vật}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|blt|ꪢ꫁ꪮꪥ|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*mɔːlʔ||human being}} (secondary borrowing from a Muong lect?). Cognate with {{cog|mtq|-}} Bi {{m|mtq|mõl||human being}}. Attested as {{m|mkh-mvi|mọi}} in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651).
{{rfe|vi|
Further origin uncertain:
*Schuessler (2007: 391,392) proposes that Vietic {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*mɔːlʔ}} is cognate to {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*c-mɔːlʔ||digging stick}}, as well as to such descendants of {{cog|mkh-pro|*jm(o:)l||male}} as {{cog|okz|jmol||male (of animals)}} (⇒ {{cog|km|ឈ្មោល}}), {{cog|omx|jmur|jmūr ~ jmur|male (elephant)}}, {{cog|sza|rəmɔːl||male}}; according to Schuessler, both "male" and "digging stick" derived from a stem represented in {{cog|kjg|tr=crmɔɔl|t=digging stick}}, {{m|kjg|tr=cmɔ:l|t=to plant (rice) with digging stick}}, and {{cog|okz|cval||to enter, penetrate, (of animals) copulate}}<ref>Schuessler, Axel (2007). ''ABC Etymological Dictionary of Old Chinese'', Honolulu: University of Hawaii Press</ref> (⇒ {{cog|km|ចូល}}).
**If so, from *'''čɑɑr''' "to dig, to delve"<ref>Ferlus, Michel. "Sur l'origine géographique des languages Viet-Muong". ''Mon-Khmer Studies'' (18-19). 1989-1990</ref> (Ferlus, 1989-1990: 54-56). Compare also {{cog|vi|xoi||to bore, to perforate}}, {{m|vi|xói}}, {{m|vi|moi}}, {{m|vi|mói||to delve, to dig out}}, which are this root's reflexes with back vowels.
*However, Ferlus did not deem Vietnamese [[mọi]] and {{cog|mtq|mõl}} to be derivatives of *'''čaar'''; instead, he relates them to {{cog|kjg|tr=hmmaːl|t=soul}} (Ferlus: 55);
**If so, {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*mɔːlʔ||human being}} would be a derivative of {{der|vi|mkh-pro|*smuul ~ smuəl ~ smaal ~ smal||shadow, soul}} (Shorto, 2006: #1779); nevertheless, Shorto did not count Vietic items among reflexes of this root.<ref>Shorto, H. ''A Mon-Khmer Comparative Dictionary'', Ed. Paul Sidwell, 2006</ref>}}

====Noun====
