If this were {{vi-etym-sino|毋|''injunctive and imperative negative''; do not, should not, must not|{{l|vi|vô}}, {{l|vi|mưu}}|hv=n|nocap=y}}, then its ''nặng''-tone (instead of expected **''huyền'') has resulted from either borrowing from a regional Chinese dialect (see {{m|vi|tạnh}}), or indirect borrowing (see {{m|vi|tiếng}}), or an irregular pre-Middle Chinese sound change (see {{m|vi|vẹn}} and {{m|vi|nhặng}}).

