nhau.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
Attested in ''Phật thuyết đại báo phụ mẫu ân trọng kinh'' (佛說大報父母恩重經) as {{m|vi|𬼀}}, the abbreviated form of {{ltc-l|饒|id=1}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|nhiêu}}). Attested as {{m|mkh-mvi|nhau}}, {{m|mkh-mvi|dau||each other}}, in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651).

Possibly arose from etymology 2 and replaced {{m|vi|chắc}} as the reciprocal marker in the non-North Central dialects, firmly established already in the Northern Old Vietnamese of ''Phật thuyết''.

{{rfe|vi|Is this really from the "placenta" sense? If so, then compare the unrelated {{ncog|zh|同胞|t=comrade|lit=same placenta}} (whence {{m|vi|đồng bào}}) for similar semantics.}}

