nhôông.raw:
===Alternative forms===
* {{q|phonemic spelling}} {{l|vi|nhông}}
* {{q|phonetic spelling}} {{l|vi|dôông}}, {{q|phonemic spelling}} {{l|vi|dông}} {{q|in North Central dialects with further ‹nh-› > ‹d-› shift}}

===Etymology===
See {{m|vi|chồng}}.

This particular dialectal form is from the proto-form with {{IPAfont|*ʄ-}}, while the dominant form {{m|vi|chồng}} is from {{IPAfont|*ɟ-}} (regular lower register tone due to voiced onset). Although implosives already gave upper register tone, thanks to comparative evidences ({{cog|thm|-}} ''pʰajoːŋ¹''), the presyllable {{IPAfont|*p-}} can further be recovered. The form with {{IPAfont|*ʄ-}} is probably the more original form: {{IPAfont|*p-ʄ- > *ʄ- > *ɟ-}}, with the non-North Central dialects derived ''chồng'' from stage 3 while the North Central form is compatible with stage 2.

Compare also the case of {{m|vi|nhông||agama}} (< {{IPAfont|*-ʄ-}}), {{m|vi|chôông||agama}} (< medial {{IPAfont|*-ɟ-}}, North Central form, unaffected by lenition) and {{m|vi|giông||salamander}} (< medial {{IPAfont|*-ɟ-}}, Northern-Southern form, affected by lenition).

