* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-nhăm.wav|a=Hanoi}}

===Etymology 1===
Northern form with the commonly seen nasalization of lateral. Compare {{m|vi|lớn}} vs. {{m|vi|nhớn}}, {{m|vi|lời}} vs. {{m|vi|nhời}}, {{m|vi|lài}} vs. {{m|vi|nhài}}, {{m|vi|lạt}} vs. {{m|vi|nhạt}}. 

This sound shift originally started as nasal assimilation within the proximity of the phoneme {{IPAfont|/m/}}: {{IPAfont|*m(V)l > /mɲ/ > /ɲ/}} (as seen even in the loanword {{m|vi|nhài}}); as {{m|vi|lăm}} almost occurs only after {{m|vi|mươi}}, the expected shift occurred.

