It originally meant "to drink" and might accept, as direct object, any drinkable liquid; "''nhậu''" ('{{l|la|bibere}} / to drink') and "''nhậu'' nước" ('{{l|la|[[aqua]]m [[potare]]}} / to drink water') were attested in ''Dictionarium Anamitico-Latinum'' ([https://archive.org/details/DictionariumAnamiticoLatinumPigneaux/Dictionarium%20Anamitico-Latinum%20-%201772%2C%20P.J.%20Pigneaux/page/n363/mode/2up 1772]; [https://web.archive.org/web/20230830174521/http://www.nomfoundation.org/nom-tools/Taberd-Dictionary?p=fulltext&item=3&view=368&uiLang=en 1838]).

