===Etymology===
{{com|vi|núi|lửa|t1=[[mountain]]|t2=[[fire]]}}, {{calque|vi|zh|火焰山|tr=hoả diệm/diễm sơn|nocap=y}}.

Texts from the early 20th-century show very limited attestation of ''hoả sơn'' {{m|zh|火山}}, the usual term for "volcano" in Chinese and other Sino-Xenic languages, much more common in Vietnamese was {{m|vi|hoả diệm sơn}}, attested in ''Đại Nam Quấc âm tự vị'' (1895) and {{m|vi|hoả diễm sơn}}, attested in ''Cách trí giáo khoa thư'' (latter half of the 1920s); in both instances ''núi lửa'' is also attested in the vicinity. See also Satō (2015).<ref>Satō, Shōta 佐藤, 章太 (2015), [https://repository.dl.itc.u-tokyo.ac.jp/records/27468 ベトナム語母語話者における漢語由来語彙と固有語彙の区別 (The Distinction between Sino-Vietnamese and Indigenous Vietnamese Words in Vietnamese Native Speakers’ Judgment)]</ref>

