ong.raw:
===Etymology===
{{inh+|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*ʔɔːŋ||honey bee}}, from {{inh|vi|aav-pro|*ʔɔːŋ||wasp; hornet}}. Cognate with {{cog|thm|ออง||wasp}}, {{cog|pac|hong||large bee, wasp}}, {{cog|bdq|ong||wasp}}, {{cog|kjg|-}} ''ʔɔːŋ'' ("wasp"), {{cog|mnw|ဟိုၚ်|tr=hang||hornet}}, {{cog|sza|-}} ''hɔŋ'' ("hornet").

Attested as Northern {{cog|mkh-mvi|a{{mkh-mvi-apex|o}}}} in ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651).

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{IPA|vi|[ʔɔŋ˧˧]|a=Hà Tĩnh}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=con|[[蜂]], [[螉]]}}

# [[bee]]

====Graphical notes====
* This term was commonly spelled with two different graphs in Nôm texts: {{m|vi|螉}} and {{m|vi|蜂}} (with a few other graphs occured in lower frequency). Etymologically, this is a native item, yet usage of {{m|vi|蜂}} indeed indicates a strong case of [[phono-semantic matching]]. As Vietnamese is predominantly a head-initial language, the terms {{m|vi|ong mật||honeybee}} and {{m|vi|mật ong||honey}} could (at least, hypothetically) be spelled {{m|vi|[[蜂]][[蜜]]}} and {{m|vi|[[蜜]][[蜂]]}} respectively, creating double pairs of [[false friend]]s with Chinese ({{ncog|zh|蜂蜜||honey}} and {{m|zh|蜜蜂||honeybee}}).

