phương ngữ.raw:
===Etymology===
{{vi-etym-sino|方|region|語|language; speech}}.

This does not seem to be in use in Chinese, Korean, and Japanese, which use {{m|vi|方言|tr=phương ngôn}} instead, a word that has significantly limited usage in Vietnamese. Perhaps a coinage based on the word {{m|zh|言語||language|tr={{m|vi|ngôn ngữ}}}}. In Chinese, {{m|zh|方語}} refers to the {{w|Phuong language}}.

In papers by Vietnamese linguists, {{m|vi|thổ ngữ}} seems to be the favored term for "dialect".

