phải.raw:
===Etymology===
{{vi-etym-sino|被|to [[suffer]]; ''passive marker''|hv=n|bị}} (Old Chinese: {{IPAchar|/*m-pʰ(r)ajʔ, m-pʰ(r)ajʔ-s, mə-pʰ(r)aj, pʰ(r)aj-s/}} in {{vi-ref|Baxter and Sagart (2014)}}, along the semantic evolution of “to have to endure; to suffer” > “have to; must” > “correct” > “right (in direction)”. It may reflect an Old Chinese pronunciation {{IPAfont|/*N-pʰ(r)ajʔ-s/}} with the loss of a nasal prefix as is also seen in other early loans (Sagart, per. comm.).

The common Vietic word for “right” is {{cog|mkh-vie-pro|*dam|*dam ~ *tam}}, whence the now-archaic {{m|vi|đăm}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-phải.wav|a=Hanoi}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-phải.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Adjective===
{{vi-adj|[[沛]], [[拜]], [[派]], [[𬆃]]}}

# {{lb|vi|often|with ''[[bên]]''}} [[right]] {{gloss|side, direction}} (in [[bên phải]])
#: {{ux|vi|Đi bên '''phải''' đường.|Go on the right side of the road.}}
#: {{ux|vi|Rẽ (tay) '''phải'''. Quẹo (tay) '''phải'''.|Turn right.}}
# [[correct]]
#: {{ux|vi|Không '''phải''' như thế.|Not so.}}
# [[obverse]]
#: {{uxi|vi|mặt '''phải''' của tấm vải|the obverse of a piece of cloth}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|correct}} {{l|vi|đúng}}, {{l|vi|chính xác}}
* {{sense|obverse}} {{l|vi|trước}}, {{l|vi|chính}}
* {{sense|the direction right}} {{l|vi|đăm}}, {{l|vi|mặt}}

====Antonyms====
* {{antsense|the direction right}} {{l|vi|trái}}
* {{antsense|correct}} {{l|vi|không}} {{l|vi|đúng}}, {{l|vi|sai}}, {{l|vi|trật}}
* {{antsense|obverse}} {{l|vi|trái}}

====Derived terms====
