===Etymology===
{{vi-etym-sino|君|monarch|無|not|戲言|to joke, to jest, to say something playfully and not in earnest}}.

Based on a quote in ''{{w|Lüshi Chunqiu}}'' (translation adapted from Knoblock & Riegel 2001):
*{{zh-x|'''天子 無 戲言'''。天子 言，則 史 書 之，工 誦 之，士 稱 之。|tr='''Thiên tử vô hí ngôn'''. Thiên tử ngôn, tắc sử thư chi, công tụng chi, sĩ xưng chi.|'''The Son of Heaven  utters no playful words'''. What the Son of Heaven says, the scribes record, the musicians chant, and the knights proclaim.|ref=Lvshi Chunqiu|3=CL-VN|collapsed=yes|nocat=y}}

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Idiom===
{{vi-idiom}}

