râm.raw:
===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*-jəm||black, dark}}. Cognate with {{cog|mtq|-}} Bi {{m|mtq|dầm||black}}, {{cog|mnw|ယောံ}}, {{cog|mlf|-}} ''ɲam'' ("black"), {{cog|pnx|-}} ''jam'' ("black").

Attested as {{m|mkh-mvi|nhâm}} and {{m|mkh-mvi|dâm}} in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651). The unusual onset change is most likely due to the taboo of mentioning {{m|vi|dâm}}. Compare {{m|vi|dâm bụt||hibiscus}}.

Genetically unrelated to {{cog|th|ร่ม}} and {{cog|zh|-}} {{ltc-l|陰}} (SV: {{m|vi|âm}}) (although could be contaminated). The original meaning of the word was "black", as recorded in minor Vietic languages and Old Vietnamese itself, not "shady".

