rượu quốc lủi.raw:
===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|vi|rượu cuốc lủi}}

===Etymology===
{{com|vi|rượu|quốc|lủi|t1=liquor|t2=state|t3=to hide out; to slip away}}. Literally "liquor which hides out from the state".

The liquor and the term originated during the early period of French colonization of Vietnam, when the act of distilling one's own liquor at home was outlawed by the colonial government. In spite of the ban, the Vietnamese continued distilling their own liquor and hid it behind tall grass, hence {{l|vi|lủi}} ("to [[hide out]]").

The {{l|vi|quốc}} part of the term is derived from {{l|vi|quốc cấm}} ("outlawed by the state" or "illegal").

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun}}

