===Etymology 2===
This is the most recognized example of the {{IPAfont|/oj > əw/}} shift in {{m|vi|Nẫu}} dialects. This shift is regular and seems to uniformly affect all items with mainstream Southern {{IPAfont|/oj/}}. It also affects at least some items with mainstream {{IPAfont|/əːj/}} through {{IPAfont|/əːj/ - /oj/}} merger, so that mainstream written {{m|vi|trời||sky, heaven}} corresponds to {{m|vi|trầu}}. The {{IPAfont|/əːj/ - /oj/}} merger was not completed before {{IPAfont|/oj > əw/}} happened, so {{m|vi|mới}} did not shift to ''*mấu''; the rest of these {{IPAfont|/əːj/}} then shifted to a velarized {{IPAfont|/əːˠ/}} (phonetically probably {{IPAfont|[əːɰ]}}) instead, see {{m|vi|trầu quơ}}.

