===Etymology 2===
Attested in ''Phật thuyết đại báo phụ mẫu ân trọng kinh'' (佛說大報父母恩重經) as {{ltc-l|阿並|}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|a}} {{m|vi|tịnh}})<ref>{{cite-thesis|year= 2019|type=PhD|author= Võ Thị Ngọc Thúy|title= Nghiên cứu chữ Nôm và tiếng Việt trong văn bản Nhị độ mai tinh tuyển|url= https://www.scribd.com/document/719366006/nghien-cuu-chu-nom-va-tieng-viet-trong-van-ban-nhi-do-mai-tinh-tuyen-917|page= 139|publisher= Trường Đại học Sư phạm Hà Nội}}</ref> and {{m|vi|并}}, a simplified form of {{ltc-l|並}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|tịnh}}). {{zh-l|*並|to be side by side}} was used possibly because of its rime and its semantic closeness to '''sánh''' ("to compare"), as ‹s-› {{IPAfont|/ʂ ~ s/}} is not known to come from {{IPAfont|/*b-/}} (see {{vi-ref|Shimizu, 2015 & 2018}}).<!--- MC 聘 phjiengH, which behaved a chongniu-IV word, became SV sính (& theoretically **thính, which is unattested) thru' the same historical phonological change which yielded doublets with th- & s- from *ph- in chongniu-IV or similar words; e.g. 匹 *phjit > SV thất & sất --->

Attested as {{m|mkh-mvi|ſánh}} in the Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum (1651).

