sông Cái.raw:
[[File:France & Colonies-1894-delta du Song-Koï.jpg|thumb|Fleuve Rouge/Song-Coï]]

===Etymology===
{{com|vi|sông|cái|t1=river|t2=mother}}, literally "mother river", or, {{com|vi|sông|cái|t1=river|t2=great, main}}, means "Great River"; both interpretations might be correct, because both meanings are from the same etymology. This word was transliterated by the French as {{m|fr|Song-Koï}} and {{m|fr|Song-Coï}}.

This was the original name of the [[Red River]], but later used to refer to many other rivers of Vietnam. May be related to other Vietnamese river names such as {{m|vi|Cái Lớn}}, {{m|vi|Cái Bé}}, {{m|vi|Cái Mép}}, {{m|vi|Cái Vùng}}, {{m|vi|Cái Tàu}} and {{m|vi|Cái Cối}}.

For some semantic parallels, compare {{ncog|cop|ⲉⲓⲉⲣⲟ|ⲡⲉⲓⲉⲣⲟ}}, {{m|cop|ⲓⲁⲣⲟ|ⲫ̀ⲓⲁⲣⲟ|the Nile}}, {{ncog|es|Río Grande}}, {{ncog|ko|한강(漢江)||Han river}} (where {{m|ko|漢}} is a phonogram used to write the native Korean morpheme for "big", see {{ncog|okm|하다〮|tr=hàtá}}).

