súp.raw:
===Etymology===
A now common corruption of {{m|vi|xúp}} that arose either by the fact that northern Vietnamese dialects have an ''x''-''s'' merger, or that people from southern Vietnam have certain degrees of [[hyperforeignism]] when attempting to imitate the spelling of the source word, the {{cog|fr|soupe}}. Hyperforeignism is not unusual in Vietnam, especially in the South where English spellings have been increasingly adopted over transcriptions.

