===Etymology===
From a neighbour language, most likely {{phono-semantic matching|vi|km|ទុរេន|notext=1}}, ultimately from {{der|vi|ms|durian}}.

According to folk etymology, from {{af|vi|sầu|t1=[[sorrow]]|riêng|t2=[[private]]|lit=one's own sorrow}}. Durian was named ''sầu riêng'' after an ancient commemorative love story from the {{w|Tây Sơn dynasty}}, in which a man that stayed faithful to his wife after death and had a strong memory of both eating the stinky-but-delicious ''tu-rên'' (durian) that represented their love at first sight.

