===Alternative forms===
* {{q|obsolete}} {{l|vi|hoại#Etymology 2}}

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
It is {{unc|vi|title=unclear}} why Vietnamese has the aspirated stop ‹th› as reflex of the Middle Chinese initial in this particular morpheme. Other Sinitic morphemes with the same initial yielded Sino-Vietnamese ‹h›, cf. {{ltc-l|畫}} ([[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|hoạ}}, {{m|vi|hoạch}}), {{ltc-l|橫|id=2}} ([[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|hoành}}), {{ltc-l|滑|id=3}} ([[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|hoạt}}). 
<!-- Could attested ‹thoại› have resulted from (1) influence of initial ‹th-› in 說 (SV: ‹thuyết›, "to speak, to talk, to discuss, to scold, etc."; 'non-'SV: ‹thốt› "to speak, to talk, to discuss, to utter, etc.") and (2) euphemistic alteration of expected **hoại, which is homophonous to SV reading ‹hoại› of 壞 "to spoil, to be spoilt, etc." -->

[[File:話 hoại reading.jpg|thumb|Tam thiên tự (1831; 20a) records the reading of {{lang|vi|話}} as {{m|vi|𱖨|tr=hoại}}.]]

