thung lũng.raw:
===Etymology===
Trần Trọng Dương (2013) proposes the proto-form {{IPAfont|/*t<sup>h</sup>lung/}} and compares this to similar cases of preinitial cluster breaking such as {{m|vi|thuồng luồng}}, {{m|vi|thằn lằn}}, and {{m|vi|thòng lọng}}, etc.<ref>Trần Trọng Dương (2013). "[https://nguvan.hnue.edu.vn/Nghi%C3%AAn-c%E1%BB%A9u/V%C4%83n-h%E1%BB%8Dc-Vi%E1%BB%87t-Nam-trung-%C4%91%E1%BA%A1i/p/giai-ma-nhung-cau-tho-sau-chu-trong-quoc-am-thi-tap-tu-nga-duong-ngu-am-hoc-lich-su-302 Giải mã những câu thơ sáu chữ trong "Quốc âm thi tập" từ ngả đường ngữ âm học lịch sử]" ''Hán-Nôm Journal''. Vol. 1. (in Vietnamese).</ref>
The etymon in question is probably derived from {{inh|vi|aav-pro|*luŋ}} (Sidwell, 2024); Shorto (2006) reconstructed a possible {{IPAfont|*-h}} coda which would be able to explain the ''ngã'' tone in {{m|vi|lũng}}. Also, compare {{cog|km|លុង}}, {{cog|vi|lủng||having a hole, be perforated}} and {{m|vi|trũng||be lower than surrounding surface}}.

{{rfe|vi|Alternatively, {{m|vi|thung}} is attested as a free morpheme in an old Nôm text so it probably came from a distinct etymon?}}

