===Etymology===
{{compound|vi|thầy|t1=teacher|sáu|t2=six}}. Prior to [[w:Pope Paul VI|Pope Paul VI]]'s ''[[motu proprio]]'' ''Ministeria quaedam'' of 15 August 1972, the deaconate was the sixth order in the [[w:Hierarchy of the Catholic Church|Church hierarchy]], above the [[subdeacon]]ate but below the [[priesthood]]. [https://web.archive.org/web/20150409102434/http://simonhoadalat.com/DIAPHAN/CacDucCha/DCVuHuyChuong/BaiGiang/53TruyenChucLMVinhSon.htm][https://web.archive.org/web/20160304104004/http://photevnusa.org/]

