===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*k-lɔːŋ||[[clear]]; [[limpid]]}}.

Attested in ''Phật thuyết đại báo phụ mẫu ân trọng kinh'' (佛說大報父母恩重經) as {{m|vi|𱷥}}, an simplified form of {{ltc-l|龍}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|long}}). Attested as {{m|mkh-mvi|tla{{mkh-mvi-apex|o}}}} in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651).

====Adjective====
{{vi-adj|[[冲]], [[工]], [[沖]], [[𳑸]], [[𬺚]], [[𤄯]], [[󰮁]], [[𤁘]], [[𬈴]]}}

# {{lb|vi|of liquid}} [[clear]] and thus [[presumably]] [[clean]]
#: {{ant|vi|đục}}
#: {{ux|vi|Nước '''trong''' mà! Uống chắc không sao đâu!|The water looks pretty clean! Probably wouldn't hurt to drink a bit!}}
# {{lb|vi|of a material}} [[translucent]] or [[transparent]]
#: {{syn|vi|trong suốt}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col3|vi|trong lành|trong sạch|trong sáng|trong suốt|trong trắng|trong trẻo|trong vắt|trong veo|trong xanh|gạn đục khơi trong}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*k-lɔːŋ||[[inside]]}}, from {{inh|vi|aav-pro|*kluːŋ|*kluːŋ ~ *kluəŋ|[[insides]]; [[belly]]}}. Cognates include {{cog|mtq|tlong}}, {{cog|scb|-}} [Rục] ''klɔːŋ¹'', {{cog|pac|callúng}}, {{cog|ssm|-}} ''kluoːŋ'', {{cog|sti|-}} ''kluŋ'', and {{cog|km|ក្នុង}}. {{doublet|vi|lòng}}, {{m|vi|tròng}} and possibly {{m|vi|nòng}}. 

Attested in ''Phật thuyết đại báo phụ mẫu ân trọng kinh'' (佛說大報父母恩重經) as {{ltc-l|工}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|công}}) and {{ltc-l|共|id=2}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|cộng}}). Attested as {{ltc-l|工}} in the work ''Đắc thú lâm tuyền thành đạo ca'' (得趣林泉成道𰙔) found in the book ''Thiền tông bản hạnh'' (禪宗本行). Attested as {{ltc-l|工}} in ''Chu dịch quốc âm ca'' (周易國音歌). Attested as {{m|mkh-mvi|tlao᷄}} in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651).

Unrelated to {{ncog|zh|-}} {{och-l|中|tr={{IPAfont|*truŋ}}}} (B-S), which is read {{m|vi|trung}} in modern Vietnamese and spelled {{m|mkh-mvi|tru᷄}} in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum''.

{{ncog|tai-pro|*klaːŋᴬ}} (whence {{cog|th|กลาง}}) and Proto-Mienic ''*ɢljaŋᴬ'' (whence {{ncog|ium|jaangh}}) might just be look-alikes.

====Preposition====
{{vi-preposition|[[工]], [[宮]], [[中]], [[共]], [[󰅩]], [[𥪝]], [[𬺘]], [[𥪞]], [[𳑴]], [[𫏽]], [[󰛍]]}}

# [[in]]; [[inside]]; [[within]] (an [[interior]] or [[enclosed]] [[space]])
#: {{uxi|vi|'''trong''' nhà/phòng|in(side) the house/room}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''trong''' tim/lòng/bụng|in one's heart|lit=inside the heart/entrails/stomach}}
# [[within]] (an [[amount]] of [[time]])
#: {{syn|vi|trong [[vòng]]}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''trong''' (vòng) 4 tiếng|within four hours}}
# in/[[among]] (a [[group]])
#: {{syn|vi|trong [[số]]}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''trong''' đám đông|in/among the crowd}}
# in (a [[place]] in [[southern]] [[Vietnam]])
#: {{uxi|vi|'''trong''' nam|someplace in southern Vietnam; "the south"}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|vi|ngoài}}

=====Graphical notes=====
* In certain modern romanization of Nôm texts where this morpheme was written with {{ltc-l|工}}, {{ltc-l|共|id=2}}, and {{ltc-l|宮}}, it is sometimes transcribed as ⟨cong⟩ or ⟨cung⟩. This is due to the misinterpretation of the nature of the graphemes: the phonological (and likely also phonetic) value of the morpheme that these graphemes represented at the time when they were first used was probably {{IPAfont|*klɔŋ<sup>A1</sup>}} (or something similar) and was the ancestor of modern ''trong'', with the medial liquid maintained until at least the end of the Middle Vietnamese period. For a similar case, compare modern {{m|vi|trả}}, {{m|vi|giả||to pay back, to return}} < {{IPAfont|*ɓlaː<sup>C1</sup>}}, used to be spelled with {{ltc-l|把}} in numerous Nôm texts. The ''*cong'' and ''*cung'' romanizations are thus nothing more than ghosts, and ought to be transcripted instead as ⟨trong⟩ (if scriptor only tries to write the modern reflex) or reconstructed {{IPAfont|*klɔŋ<sup>A1</sup>}} (for historical value).

