trò.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
Attested as {{m|mkh-mvi|tlò}} in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651).

As shown by the Middle Vietnamese form and as well as usage of {{ltc-l|路}} as phonetic in Nôm texts, the earlier form of this word had initial cluster and can not be derived from {{ltc-l|徒}}.

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|[[路]], [[󱙞]], [[󱼒]], [[徒]], [[𠻀]]}}

# [[trick]]; [[artifice]]; [[antic]]
#: {{uxi|vi|Làm '''trò''' gì vậy?|What '''trickery''' are you doing?}}
# [[comedy]]; [[amusement]]
#: {{uxi|vi|{{w|lang=vi|Tấn '''trò''' đời}}|{{w|La Comédie humaine|La '''Comédie''' humaine ("The Human '''Comedy'''")}} ({{ng|a collection of novels and stories by {{w|Honoré de Balzac}}}})}}
# [[play]]; [[game]]; [[facetiousness]]

=====Derived terms=====
{{col3|vi|trò chuyện|trò trống|vai trò|chuyện trò|quản trò|trò đùa|giở trò|ra trò|nhà trò|trò hề|trò mèo|tích trò}}

===Etymology 2===
{{rfe|vi|Not {{ltc-l|徒}} ([[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|đồ}}). Probably the same etymon as the one above.}}

====Noun====
{{vi-noun}}

# {{short for|vi|học trò||[[pupil]]}}

====Pronoun====
{{vi-pronoun|[[路]], [[󱙞]], [[󱼒]], [[徒]], [[𠻀]]}}

# {{lb|vi|dated}} [[you]] {{q|used by a [[teacher]] when talking to a [[student]] in their [[class]]}}
#* {{quote-book|vi|year= 1997|author= {{w|J. K. Rowling}}|translator2= {{lw|vi|Lý Lan}}|title= {{w|Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone}}|newversion= Vietnamese translation from|title2= {{lw|vi|Harry Potter và Hòn đá Phù thủy}}|chapter= 11|chapter2= 11
|origtext= en:Unfortunately, something about their guilty faces caught Snape's eye. He limped over. He hadn’t seen the fire, but he seemed to be looking for a reason to tell them off anyway. “What’s that '''you'''’ve got there, Potter?”
|text= Xui xẻo là những bộ mặt… tội lỗi của chúng làm thầy Snape để ý. Thầy cà nhắc lê chân tới. Thầy không nhìn thấy ngọn lửa, nhưng có vẻ như thầy đang cố tìm ra một chuyện gì đó để mà la rầy bọn nhỏ. “'''Trò''' cầm cái gì đó, Potter?”|year2= 2006|publisher2= Nhà Xuất Bản Trẻ}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Although the use of ''trò'' as a pronoun is pretty much non-existent in current spoken Vietnamese as it is seen as too distant and formal, it is still commonly used and seen in translation works from other languages, especially Western literature.

