{{col3|vi|trống rỗng|trống trải|trống trơn|trống vắng|trống trếnh|trống trơ|vườn không nhà trống}}

===Etymology 2===
Cognate with {{cog|tou|-}} [Cuối Chăm] ''kʰrɔːŋ³''. Compare {{m|vi|sống}} as in the compound {{m|vi|sống mái}}.

The form ''sống'' was attested in numerous texts written in the Northern dialects well into the early 20th century, although just primarily in ''gà sống''. The ‹s-›-‹tr-› correspondence indicates that the now dominant form ''trống'' originated from the North Central region (compare pairs such as {{m|vi|sừng}} vs. {{m|vi|trừng||horn}}, {{m|vi|sâu}} vs. {{m|vi|trâu||caterpillar}}, {{m|vi|sành}} vs. {{m|vi|trèng||terracotta}}).

====Alternative forms====
* {{q|Northern Vietnam}} {{l|vi|sống}}

====Adjective====
{{vi-adj|[[𪟤]], [[𩀳]]}}

# {{lb|vi|of a bird}} [[male]]
#: {{ant|vi|mái}}
#: {{uxi|vi|gà '''trống'''|a rooster}}
# {{lb|vi|of an animal with {{m|vi|cá||fish}} in its name|including cetaceans}} [[male]]
#: {{ant|vi|mái}}
#: {{uxi|vi|cá heo '''trống'''/đực|a male dolphin}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Less common than {{m|vi|đực}} when used for "fish", although it is not rare nor uncommon.

=====Derived terms=====
{{col|vi|gà trống nuôi con}}

====See also====
* {{vi-l|đực}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-mvi|tlóu᷃}}. Cognate with {{cog|scb|-}} [Mày] {{m|scb|klống}}, {{m|scb|klôống}}, {{cog|scb|-}} [Mã Liềng] {{m|scb|klống}} ({{vi-ref|Trần Trọng Dương, 2014}}). Of {{bor|vi|tai}} origin; compare {{cog|tai-pro|*kloːŋᴬ}}, whence {{cog|th|กลอง}}, {{cog|lo|ກອງ}}, {{cog|za|gyong}}. 

Attested in ''Quốc âm thi tập'' (國音詩集; 15th cent.) as {{m|vi|𫪹}}, composed of {{ltc-l|古}} + {{ltc-l|弄}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|cổ}} {{m|vi|lộng}}). Attested in ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651) as Northern {{inh|vi|mkh-mvi|tlóũ}}.

