tấy.raw:
===Etymology===
See {{m|vi|rái}}.

In spite of a phonological discrepancy, ''rái'' and ''tấy'' are both regular reflexes of the Proto-Vietic word in terms of dialectal development, wih most Vietnamese dialects spirantized medial ''*-s-'' to ‹r› while the North Central dialects kept the ''*-s-'' (that later regularly shifted to ‹t›) unaffected by the presyllable ''*p-''. For the ‹ay›-‹ây› (< ''*eː'') correspondence, compare North Central {{m|vi|gấy}} vs. standard written {{m|vi|gái}}, {{m|vi|trấy}} vs. {{m|vi|trái}}, {{m|vi|cây}} vs. {{m|vi|gai}}.

