tỏi.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{vi-etym-sino|蒜|garlic|hv=n|toán}}.

Compare {{cog|zhn|soiq||garlic}}. To account for the glide reflex in both languages, the borrowed Sinitic word was probably a dialectal form where earlier {{IPAfont|*-r-s}} shifted to {{IPAfont|*-jH}} instead of the typical {{IPAfont|*-nH}} (if the word was borrowed independently when the liquid still presented, Vietnamese would have {{IPAfont|*-j}} while Nong Zhuang would have {{IPAfont|*-n}}). However, it is also possible that there was borrowing involved: if the direction was Vietic > Tai, the Chinese form could be an early form with {{IPAfont|*-r-s}} (> {{IPAfont|*-lʰ > -jC}}) or a later form with {{IPAfont|*-jH}}; if the direction was Tai > Vietic, the borrowed Sinitic form must be {{IPAfont|*-jH}}.

See also {{m|vi|tươi}}, from {{ncog|zh|鮮}}, with modern {{IPAfont|-j}}.

