tụi.raw:
===Etymology===
From a form of {{der|vi|zh|-}} {{ltc-l|對||pair}} ([[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|đối}}) in a southern Sinitic lect. Southern Min lects ({{m|nan-tws|對}} or {{m|nan-hbl|對}}) are phonetically close, but in these lects, the word for "pair" is usually {{ltc-l|雙}}; in Yue, {{m|yue|對}} is the chief word for "pair" but phonetically it is less straightforward as far as the prestigious {{w|Yuehai Yue|Guangfu}} lects are concerned. In any case, {{doublet|vi|đôi|nocap=y}}.

In ''Đại Nam quấc âm tự vị'' (1895), ''tụi'' was glossed as {{m|vi|[Đ]ôi, [[cặp]], [[bọn]]||pair, couple, bunch}}.

