===Etymology 2===
{{rfe|vi|{{vi-etym-sino|比||hv=no|tỉ}}, short for {{vi-l|tỉ-khâu-ni|比丘尼}} < {{cog|pi|bhikkhunī}} < {{cog|sa|भिक्षुणी}}? <!--- PhanAnh123's commentary: I know about the distinction between Chongniu III and IV in Sino-Vietnamese, cases of relabialization of SV reading for Chongniu IV characters that should have shown palatalization, like {{m|vi|Diến Điện}} or {{m|vi|diên man}}, as well as cases of vernacular loans that have labial onsets while SV readings have palatalization ({{m|vi|bèn}}, {{m|vi|bít tất}}, etc.) but why would ''vãi'' here have lenition? There is {{m|vi|ví}} for that same character, with actually regular tonal correspondence for an early loan, for the tonal correspondence of ''vãi'' to make sense, it needs to be a rather late loan, but in that case, the preinitial should already disappear and along with it the environment for lenition. --->}}

