văn ngôn.raw:
{{swp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
{{vi-etym-sino|文言}}.

Prior to the post-colonial period, the commonly used term for [[Classical Chinese]] was [[Hán văn]]. During the twentieth century, văn ngôn increasingly came to be used as a more specific linguistic distinction for Classical/Literary Chinese, in contrast with bạch thoại (vernacular Chinese). This is also due to the fact that present Vietnamese are learning Mandarin Chinese instead of Classical Chinese.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun}}

# [[Literary Chinese]] {{gl|literary language used from the fall of the {{w|Han dynasty}} (220 {{C.E.}}) to the early 20th century}}
# [[Classical Chinese]] {{gl|literary language used in old China}}
#: {{syn|vi|cổ văn|Hán văn}}

===Proper noun===
{{vi-propn}}

# name of a section in the ''{{w|Ten Wings}}'' in the ''{{w|Book of Changes}}''
#* {{quote-book|vi|year=1815|title=周易解義演歌<tr:Chu dịch giải nghĩa diễn ca>|trans-title=Versified Explanation of the Meanings of the Zhou Yi|volume=1|pages=5b–6a|url=https://lib.nomfoundation.org/collection/1/volume/919/page/39|passage=𠳒'''《文言》'''浪：「元」意，羅蒸奇德冷丕；「亨」意，𦉼蒸合德卒丕；「利」意，𦉼蒸和𱻊丕；「貞」意，𦉼蒸㭲役丕。㝵君子体德仁都黙𫜵奇㝵，冷合都黙合礼，利物都黙和𱻊，恒𥾽都黙𢧚役。㝵君子𫜵𦊚德意，爲丕浪：「乾、元、亨、利、貞」。|tr=Lời '''Văn Ngôn''' rằng: "Nguyên" ấy, là chưng cả đức lành vậy; "Hanh" ấy, là chưng hợp đức tốt vậy; "Lợi" ấy, là chưng hòa nghĩa vậy; "Trinh" ấy, là chưng gốc việc vậy. Người quân tử thấy đức nhân đủ mặc làm cả người, lành hợp đủ mặc hợp lễ, lợi vật đủ mặc hòa nghĩa, hằng bền đủ mặc nên việc. Người quân tử làm bốn đức ấy, vì vậy rằng: "Càn (Kiền), nguyên, hanh, lợi, trinh".|t=The '''Wenyan commentary''' says: Yuan is the chief of all goodness; Heng is the gathering of what is good; Li is the harmonization of righteousness; Zhen is the foundation of affairs. The junzi embodies benevolence and is therefore able to take charge of others; he brings together what is good and is able to accord with ritual propreity; he benefits others and is able to harmonize righteousness; he is upright and is able to serve as a foundation of affairs. The junzi practices these four virtues; therefore it can be said: "Qian: Yuan, Heng, Li, Zhen".}}

