===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|vi|map}}. Compare {{cog|ms|ribu||thousand}}, {{cog|cjm|ribau}}, {{m|cjm|rabau||thousand}}. Also borrowed from the same source are {{cog|bdq|rơbâu||thousand}}, {{cog|kpm|röböu||hundred thousand}}.

The meaning in ''Dictionarium Anamitico-Latinum'' (1838) is defined as "one million", but in ''Như Tây nhựt trình'' (1889), it clearly means "one hundred thousand".

This word seems to be a South Central-Southern item, while the Northern dialects chiefly used {{vi-link|ức||億}}. 

