===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*viːt||duck}}. Compare {{cog|ncb|-}} [Nancowry] {{m|ncb|wet||duck}}.

Alves ([http://pacling.anu.edu.au/series/SEALS-PDFs/alves2015etyma.pdf 2015]) suggests a Proto-Tai origin (compare {{cog|tai-pro|*pitᴰ}}, and {{cog|qfa-lic-pro|*ɓit}}, Proto-Ong-Be *''ɓit<sup>D1</sup>''). Although he later (Alves, 2021) expresses doubt towards the details of direction of borrowing. These items might just imitative, so there was no borrowing involved from any direction.<!-- It's unlikely from phonological standpoint anyway, the Kra-Dai side clearly points to a stop, while Vietic consistent has *v- (Proto-Vietic had both *p- and *v-). -->

Compare also {{zh-l|*鴄}} ([[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|thất}}).

