xin lỗi.raw:
{{phrasebook|vi}}

===Etymology===
{{compound|vi|xin|t1=to beg|lỗi|t2=mistake}}.

The literal meaning of these two words is "''to [[beg]] for [[someone]]'s [[mistake]]''", which some people might consider strange. It's possibly a shortened form of the more [[outdate]]d [[literary]] form {{m|vi|xin}} {{m|vi|thứ lỗi}}/{{m|vi|xin}} {{m|vi|tha thứ|tha}} {{m|vi|lỗi}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Verb===
{{vi-verb|吀纇}}

# to [[apologise]]

===Interjection===
{{vi-interj|吀纇}}

# [[I'm sorry]] (for my [[mistake]]/[[transgression]])
#: {{ux|vi|Xin lỗi, tớ không cố ý.|Sorry, I didn't mean to do that.}}
# {{lb|vi|polite}} [[excuse me]]/[[pardon me]] (for [[intruding]]/[[disturbing]] you)
#: {{ux|vi|Xin lỗi, cho hỏi đây có phải là nhà anh Tiến không ạ?|Excuse me, is this Mr. Tiến's address?}}

====Usage notes====
* For the English phrase {{m|en|I'm sorry|pos=about your loss / about this inconvenience / what you've been through}}, translators may use {{m|vi|[[rất]] [[tiếc]] / [[tiếc]] [[quá]]||that's a pity}} or {{m|vi||xin chia buồn với...|my condolences to...}}.
**{{ux|vi|'''Rất tiếc''', chúng tôi hết phòng đôi rồi ạ.|I'm sorry, we have run out of twin rooms.}}
* To ask for pardon and understanding in more mild contexts, {{m|vi||xin [[bỏ qua]]|forgive}} or {{m|vi|xin [[thông cảm]]||sympathize}} may be used instead.
**{{ux|vi|Nếu video có gì sai sót mong quý khán thính giả '''bỏ qua'''.|If there are any errors in this video, I hope the audience will forgive.}}
**{{ux|vi|Xin '''thông cảm''' mình đã trễ vì sáng nay bị kẹt xe.|Please be understanding for having been late because of traffic this morning.}}

