Analyzed as {{com|vi|áo|bà|ba}}, lit. "[[shirt]] of the [[third]] (born) [[madam]]". According to {{w|Sơn Nam (nhà văn)|Sơn Nam|lang=vi}}, named after the dress of the {{w|Baba Nyonya}} aka [[Peranakan]]s (ethnic Chinese from Penang, Malaysia).

