ăn trắng mặc trơn.raw:
===Etymology===
{{compound|vi|ăn|trắng|mặc|trơn|t1=to eat|t2=white|t3=to wear|t4=smooth; polished}}. 
The term refers to the luxury of eating polished white rice (as opposed to coarse grains) and wearing fine, smooth fabrics like silk.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-ipa}}

===Idiom===
{{head|vi|idiom|head=[[ăn]] [[trắng]] [[mặc]] [[trơn]]}}

# {{lb|vi|idiomatic}} to [[live]] a [[life]] of [[leisure]], [[comfort]], and [[wealth]]
# to be [[accustomed]] to a [[high]] [[standard of living]] without having to perform [[manual]] [[labor]]
#: {{ux|vi|Cả đời chỉ biết '''ăn trắng mặc trơn''', chẳng hiểu gì về nỗi khổ của người nông dân.|Having lived in the '''lap of luxury''' all their life, they understand nothing of the farmers' hardships.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|vi|ăn sung mặc sướng}}
* {{l|vi|vinh hoa phú quý}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|vi|đầu tắt mặt tối}} (to be busy and overworked)
* {{l|vi|chân lội bùn, tay cấy mạ}} (to perform hard manual labor)
* {{l|vi|ăn mắm mút dòi}}

ăn to nói lớn.raw:
===Etymology===
{{compound|vi|[[ăn]]|[[to]]|[[nói]]|[[lớn]]|t1=to eat|t2=big|t3=to speak|t4=large}}. Literally, “to eat big, to speak big”.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-ipa}}

===Idiom===
{{head|vi|idiom|head=[[ăn]] [[to]] [[nói]] [[lớn]]}}

# {{lb|vi|idiomatic}} to be [[straightforward]], [[bold]], and [[decisive]] in one's [[conduct]] and [[speech]]
# to [[act]] with [[confidence]] and [[magnanimity]]; to have a [[strong]] and [[forthright]] [[personality]]
#: {{ux|vi|Tính ông ấy vốn '''ăn to nói lớn''', không thích sự rụt rè.|He is by nature '''bold and straightforward'''; he doesn't like hesitancy.}}

====Usage notes====
* This idiom usually carries a positive or neutral connotation, describing someone who is honest and robust. It is often associated with people from rural, military, or working-class backgrounds who lack pretension.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|vi|hào sảng}}
* {{l|vi|thẳng thắn}}
* {{l|vi|thẳng như ruột ngựa}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|vi|ăn nhỏ nói khẽ}}
* {{l|vi|khép nép}}

ăn tục nói phét.raw:
===Etymology===
{{compound|vi|[[ăn]]|[[tục]]|[[nói]]|[[phét]]|t1=to eat; to behave|t2=vulgar; obscene|t3=to speak|t4=to brag; to lie}}. Literally, “to eat vulgarly and speak boastfully”.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-ipa}}

===Idiom===
{{head|vi|idiom|head=[[ăn]] [[tục]] [[nói]] [[phét]]}}

# {{lb|vi|idiomatic|derogatory}} to [[habitually]] [[use]] [[foul]] [[language]] and [[tell]] [[tall tales]] or [[lies]]
# to [[be]] [[unrefined]], [[vulgar]], and [[dishonest]] in [[one's]] [[speech]] and [[conduct]]
#: {{ux|vi|Loại người chuyên '''ăn tục nói phét''' như hắn thì chẳng ai coi trọng.|People like him, who are always '''vulgar and bragging''', are never respected.}}

====Usage notes====
* This idiom is strongly derogatory and is used to criticize a person's character, specifically their lack of refinement and integrity.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|vi|ba hoa chích chòe}} {{qualifier|specifically for bragging}}
* {{l|vi|nói láo}}
* {{l|vi|xạo lồn}} {{qualifier|slang; vulgar}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|vi|nói có sách, mách có chứng}} (to speak with evidence)

