===Etymology===
{{etydate|1479}} in ''[[Đại Việt sử ký toàn thư]]'', in [[chữ Hán]] form {{l|vi|大瞿越}}.

Momoki (2014) proposes that {{l|vi|大瞿越|tr=Đại Cồ Việt}} likely derives from the vernacular form {{m|vi|Cự Việt}} ({{l|vi|鉅越}} & {{l|vi|巨越}}) as recorded in two {{w|Lý dynasty}}'s inscriptions, or {{m|vi|Kẻ Việt}}, instead of the state's 10th-century name, as the form {{l|vi|大越|tr=Đại Việt}} had been attested earlier in 10th-century brick inscriptions.<ref>Momoki Shiro (2014), "The Vietnamese empire and its expansion, ''c''.980–1840". In ''Asian Expansions: The Historical Experiences of Polity Expansion in Asia'', edited by Geoff Wade, p. 158. London: Routledge.</ref>

