Đồng Nai.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Etymology===
Per folk/surface etymology, from {{com|vi|đồng|t1=[[field]]|nai|t2=[[deer]]|lit=Field of Deer}}. Alternatively, from the {{der|vi|cma|-}} word for "river" (comparable to {{cog|kpm|đờng}}) and the word ''nai'' above, if so, originally referred to the {{w|Đồng Nai River}}. 

Even if the surface etymology is faulty, it was popular enough that {{m|zh|鹿野|tr=Lộc Dã}} became one of the {{m|vi|tên chữ||literary name}} of the region. See also {{m|vi|Đồng Xoài}} and {{m|vi|Đồng Tháp}}, although it is not clear if the ''Đồng'' there are related to that of ''Đồng Nai'' (or even to each other) or not.

Compare also {{m|vi|Hố Nai|lit=Deer Pit}} (at least superficially), the name of a ward of {{m|vi|Biên Hoà}}, the capital city of Đồng Nai, and a likely related toponym.

