{{vi-IPA}}

===Pronoun===
{{vi-pronoun|[[帝]], [[啼]], [[蒂]], [[帶]], [[𢃄]], [[𦷾]]}}

# {{lb|vi|Northern Vietnam|usually|informal}} [[there]], [[that]] [[place]], [[that]]
#: {{syn|vi|đó}}

====Usage notes====
* In the Southern dialects, {{m|vi|đó}} is usually preferred.

{{box-top|Grammar}}
* The [[demonstrative pronoun]] ''đấy'' ("there, that") denotes a place, person or thing far from the speaker, but close to whom the speaker is talking to. When denoting a place, ''đấy'' refers to either a location or a movement to the location.
:: {{uxi|vi|Họ đang [[tập]] [[bóng chuyền]] ở '''đấy'''.|They are practicing volleyball there. (location)}}
:: {{uxi|vi|[[đừng|Đừng]] đi đến '''đấy''' vào [[ban đêm]]. [[nguy hiểm|Nguy hiểm]] lắm.|Do not go there at night. It is very unsafe. (movement to the location)}}
* The destination for {{m|vi|đi}} in the "''đi'' + preposition + destination" construction can be expressed by ''đấy'' ("there") and is treated as a noun.

* ''Đấy'' can serve as the [[subject]] of the sentence containing the [[predicate noun]].
:: {{uxi|vi|'''Đấy''' là bạn tôi.|'''That''' is my friend.}}

* [[indefinite pronoun|Indefinite pronouns]] and adverbs are formed by placing a question word before the demonstrative ''đấy'': {{m|vi|ai}} ''đấy'' ("someone"), {{m|vi|cái gì}} ''đấy'' ("something"), {{m|vi|ở đâu}} ''đấy'' ("somewhere"), {{m|vi|khi nào}} ''đấy'' ("sometime"), {{m|vi|nơi}} ''nào đấy'' ("somewhere, someplace, in some place"), {{m|vi|người}} ''nào đấy'' ("someone").

* ''Đấy'' and {{m|vi|đâu}} are also adverbs of place and can be [[semantically]] paired to form a similarity clause.
:: {{uxi|vi|Chị đi '''đâu''', tôi đi đến '''đấy''' với chị.|Wherever you go, I will come with you.}}

* ''Đấy'' is used after a preposition to refer to an action or event that has just been mentioned.
:: {{ux|vi|Tôi học [[cao học]] về [[Việt Nam học]]. <u>Trước</u> '''đấy''' ở [[bậc]] [[đại học]] tôi [[chuyên]] về [[Đông Nam Á]] học.|I did my master's degree in Vietnamese studies, and before that as an undergraduate I majored in Southeast Asian studies.}}
* In recent years, the demonstrative pronoun ''đấy'' is used in the Hanoi dialect with the function of the demonstrative adjective {{m|vi|ấy}}, for instance: {{m|vi|kĩ sư}} ''đấy'', ''cái'' {{m|vi|áo}} ''đấy'', ''bộ'' {{m|vi|phim}} ''đấy''.
{{box-bottom}}

====See also====
{{vi-demonstratives}}

===Particle===
{{vi-particle}}

# {{lb|vi|northern Vietnam}} {{n-g|[[sentence]]-[[final]] [[particle]] used in [[question]]s for asking in a more [[polite]] way}}
#: {{ux|vi|Anh đang chờ ai '''đấy'''?|Who are you waiting for?}}
# {{lb|vi|northern Vietnam}} {{n-g|[[sentence]]-[[final]] [[particle]] in [[statement]]s to [[express]] [[affirmation]]}}
#: {{ux|vi|[[máy bay|Máy bay]] của họ [[hạ cánh]] rồi '''đấy'''.|Their airplane has in fact landed.}}

====Usage notes====
* When used in questions, ''đấy'' can be replaced by {{m|vi|thế}}. In the Southern dialects, ''đó'' is used instead of ''đấy'' and {{m|vi|vậy}} instead of ''thế''.
* When expressing affirmation, the meaning of ''đấy'' is similar to the English "actually" or "in fact". In the Southern dialects, ''đó'' is used instead of ''đấy''.

