đệ.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{vi-etym-sino|第|[[ordinal]] [[marker]]}}.

====Prefix====
{{vi-prefix}}

# {{lb|vi|only before Sino-Vietnamese numerals}} {{n-g|[[ordinal]] [[number]] [[marker]], used only to mark the generation of a person who shares their name, equivalent to the use of I, II, III, etc. in English. In actual practice, mostly used for royal designations and titles.}}
#: {{syn|vi|thứ}}
# {{lb|vi|only before Sino-Vietnamese numerals|rare}} {{n-g|[[ordinal]] [[number]] [[marker]] in general}}
#: {{uxi|vi|Đệ Tam Quốc tế|the {{w|Communist International|Third International}}}}
#: {{uxi|vi|Đệ Nhất Phu nhân|the First Lady}}

=====Usage notes=====
* ''Đệ'' is in regular use for ordinal numbers in lower than tenth in royal designations, thus {{w|Charles III}} is ''Charles Đệ Tam''. 
* For eleventh and above, even in royal designations, {{m|vi|thứ}} would be preferred. For example, {{w|Louis XIV}} would probably be read as ''Louis Thứ Mười bốn'', not ''*Louis Đệ Thập tứ''.

