đểu.raw:
===Etymology===
In ''Dictionnaire Annamite-Français'' (1898), J. F. M. Génibrel glosses "gánh ['''đểu''']" as "{{l|fr|[[porter]] des [[fardeau]]x||to carry [with a shoulder pole] burdens ~ loads"}} and "{{lang|vi|thằng ['''đểu''']}}"  as "{{l|fr|portefaix||{{l|en|porter}} (n.)}}", suggesting that ''đểu'' originally meant "load, burden" → "person who carries burdens or loads, porter".<ref name = "daf-deu">{{cite-book|author= J.F.M. Génibrel|year= 1898|title= Dictionnaire Annamite-Français|entry= Đểu|page= 211|pageurl= https://chunom.org/pages/genibrel/#211}}</ref> Further etymology unknown; still, compare {{zh-l|挑|to carry [something] with a shoulder pole}}.

{{w|Vương Trung Hiếu}} (2021) proposes that ''đểu'' initially meant "{{lang|vi|người gánh thuê}} ('hired porter using [[carrying pole]]')" and presents an unsourced viewpoint that ''đểu'' nowadays means "caddish" because poorly-educated porters often dealt unfairly with one another and competed against each other for customers by means of cheating and violence.<ref>{{cite-web|vi|author= Vương Trung Hiếu|year= 2021|url= https://thanhnien.vn/lat-leo-chu-nghia-deu-cang-va-cuu-van-post1403367.html|title=Lắt léo chữ nghĩa: ‘Đểu cáng’ và ‘cửu vạn’|trans-title= Conundrum about Words and Meanings: ‘Đểu cáng’ and ‘cửu vạn’|work= {{w|Thanh Niên}}|trans-work= Young People}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Adjective===
{{vi-adj|[[搗]], [[𢞬]]}}

# {{lb|vi|derogatory}} [[ill-bred]]; [[unmannerly]]; [[caddish]]

====Derived terms====
