đứt.raw:
===Etymology===
{{inh+|vi|aav-pro|*tacʔ||to break, to sever}}. Cognate with {{cog|mtq|-}} Bi {{m|mtq|tếch}}, {{cog|km|ដាច់}}, {{cog|kpm|tac||to cut}}, {{cog|hal|kơtĕk||to snap, to break (rope)}}, {{cog|kha|thait||to snap}}, {{cog|kjg|-}} ''tec'' ("torn raggedly"). {{doublet|vi|dứt}}.

Attested in ''Quốc âm thi tập'' (國音詩集; {{circa2|15th cent.|short=1}}) as {{m|vi|󱢎}}, composed of {{ltc-l|悉}} + {{ltc-l|个}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|tất}} {{m|vi|cá}}), preserving earlier {{IPAfont|*k-t-}} onset cluster. The sound shift from proto-form {{IPAfont|/*s-/}} > modern {{IPAfont|/t-/}} must have already completed by this point in time. 

