𠬠.raw:
[[File:Evolution of 沒 to 𠬠 (NoCareBearsGiven).jpg|alt=Evolution of 'một': 沒 → * → 𱥺 → 𠬠 (*: the cursive form of "沒", essentially simplifies the "勹" part with the "丷" part, before the water radical, 氵, is removed to simplify more). |border|right|277x277px|'''Evolution of 'một', from 沒 to 𠬠 (Image by NoCareBearsGiven).''']]

===Glyph origin===
Simplified from {{m|vi|𱥺}}, itself a variant of {{m|vi|沒|tr={{vi-l|một}}}}. See also {{m|vi|𰰝}} and {{m|vi|𠬛}}.

Beginning from the 18th century, {{m|vi|蔑}} was displaced as the common character for một ("[[one]]") being replaced by {{m|vi|沒|tr={{vi-l|một}}}}.<ref>{{quote-book|vi|author=Trần Trọng Dương|title=Lý thuyết và thực hành chữ Nôm|trans-title=A Textbook on Vietnamese Nom Script|page=88|passage=Số một: từ thế kỷ XVIII về trước viết là 蔑 (AHV: miệt). Sau viết bằng 沒 một, tục thể viết là 𱥺. Chữ này được viết tắt thành 殳 , tục thể viết là 𠬠. Chữ mốt cũng được ghi như vậy.|year=2016|isbn=9786046257264|translation=(Number) One: "蔑" (SV: "miệt") was used prior to the 18th century. Later, it was written as "沒" (SV: một), with the vulgar form as "𱥺". This character was then simplified to "殳", with the vulgar form as "𠬠"; "mốt" is also written that way.}}</ref>

