𢈱.raw:
===Glyph origin===
Phonetic compound ({{m|vi|hội âm}}/{{m|vi|chữ kép}}; {{lang|vi|會音}}/{{lang|vi|𡨸甲}}): abbreviated phonetic {{m|vi|麻|tr={{vi-l|ma}}}} + phonetic {{m|vi|利|tr={{vi-l|lợi}}}}.

This character was based on the ancient form of {{m|vi|lời}} (recorded in {{ncog|mkh-mvi|-}} as {{m|mkh-mvi|mlời}}). Some of its earliest attestations are found in ''Thiên Nam ngữ lục ngoại kỷ'' ({{lang|vi|天南語籙外紀}}; 17th or 18th century), and it continued to be used until the 20th century in works such as ''Sãi vãi tân lục quốc âm diễn ca'' ({{lang|vi|仕𠉜新錄国音演𰙔}}) and several versions of ''{{w|Lục Vân Tiên}}'' (including the 1874 and 1916 versions).

See also {{m|vi|𠅜}}, another double phonogram for {{m|vi|lời}} that was first attested in earlier texts.

